\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah hits 2-week high as Indonesia c.bank meets after fuel hike\b0\par\par\uc2 739 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2014\par 05:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Indonesia fuel price hike to save govt $8 bln in 2015\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  starts monetary policy meeting\par     * Some expect rate hike on higher inflation\par     * Some predict no change amid growth worries\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 18 (Reuters) - Indonesia's rupiah hit a\par two-week high on Tuesday, with some expectations that its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will raise interest rates    a day after President\par Joko Widodo announced a long-awaited increase in subsidised fuel\par prices.\par     The increases of more than 30 percent are expected to save\par the government of Southeast Asia's biggest economy more than $8\par billion next year, and help bring down both the fiscal and\par current account deficits. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  (BI) started an unscheduled meeting earlier\par on Tuesday to discuss monetary policy, as the rise in fuel\par prices is expected to add 2 percentage points to the annual\par inflation rate this year.\par     The rupiah earlier rose as much as 0.8 percent to\par 12,100 per dollar, its strongest since Nov. 5. \par     Jakarta shares gained 0.5 percent.\par     "The fuel price hike delivered in Indonesia should be\par welcomed by the market," said Jonathan Cavenagh, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Singapore.\par     "This will no doubt fuel expectation of a fresh rate hike,\par which the market has not generally been looking for," Cavenagh\par said, referring to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's extra policy meeting.\par     A surprise rate hike could lift one-month non-deliverable\par forwards (NDFs) for the rupiah to 12,000-12,100\par per dollar, he added. The NDFs stood at 12,168 as of 0400 GMT,\par compared with its previous close of 12,170.\par     Economists were split over whether the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will\par raise its policy rate by 25 basis points or leave it unchanged,\par for fear it could dampen economic growth.\par     "BI has limited room to raise rates, in our view, because of\par the slowdown in growth, which will be exacerbated by this fiscal\par tightening," Nomura said in a note to clients, adding it expects\par no rate hike until December at the earliest.\par     Nomura said it expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  confine itself to\par reiterating that it stands ready to increase rates if there are\par signs that impact causes persistent inflation pressures.\par     It also took a cautious stance on the rupiah, saying the the\par fuel price hike in and broadly stronger dollar were priced in.\par     Spot rupiah pared some of earlier gains to standat 12,150.\par     \par     WON\par     The won fell on growing caution over possible\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to\par check the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength against the yen.\par     Taking its cue from the yen's recovery, the won erased some\par of its earlier losses as stop-loss dollar selling emerged.\par     Still, caution over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  increased as the South\par Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hovered a near six-year high against\par the yen, and some offshore funds sold the won, traders said.\par     On Monday, the won hit 9.3986 to the yen, its strongest\par since August 2008.\par     A weakening yen raises concern that South Korea would lose\par competitiveness against Japan as the two countries compete to\par export a similar range of products, notably cars and electronic\par goods.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0400 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       116.59         116.65       +0.05\par   Sing dlr        1.2969         1.2981       +0.09\par   Taiwan dlr      30.709         30.739       +0.10\par   Korean won     1098.50        1093.90       -0.42\par   Baht             32.76          32.78       +0.05\par   Peso             44.94          44.89       -0.10\par   Rupiah        12150.00       12202.00       +0.43\par   Rupee            61.83          61.73       -0.16\par   Ringgit         3.3500         3.3470       -0.09\par   Yuan            6.1231         6.1241       +0.02\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       116.59         105.28       -9.70\par   Sing dlr        1.2969         1.2632       -2.60\par   Taiwan dlr      30.709         29.950       -2.47\par   Korean won     1098.50        1055.40       -3.92\par   Baht             32.76          32.86       +0.31\par   Peso             44.94          44.40       -1.20\par   Rupiah        12150.00       12160.00       +0.08\par   Rupee            61.83          61.80       -0.05\par   Ringgit         3.3500         3.2755       -2.22\par   Yuan            6.1231         6.0539       -1.13\par     \par \par  (Edi