\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won leads Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  gains as yen rebounds despite Japan's slump\b0\par\par\uc2 746 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2014\par 05:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Won gains on exporters, chart support at 1,104.3/dlr\par     * Baht up after hawkish c.bank; weaker GDP ignored\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 17 (Reuters) - South Korea's won led gains in\par emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday as the yen rebounded from a\par seven-year low struck after data showed Japan's economy\par unexpectedly slipped into recession, hitting Tokyo stocks.\par     The won recovered from a 14-month trough to\par outperform regional units as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is more sensitive to\par the yen than its peers.\par     The Thai baht gained as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lowered\par expectations for an interest rate cut, even though third quarter\par economic growth missed expectations. \par  \par     The Japanese data showed the world's third largest economy\par contracted an annualised 1.6 percent in the third quarter, \par reinforcing expectations that Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shinzo Abe\f28 \uc2 \f2  will\par call a snap election and delay a second sales tax hike next\par year. \par     The data initially pushed the yen down to a\par seven-year low against the dollar. The yen, however, reversed\par course as slumping Tokyo shares prompted investors to\par unwind short positions. Many investors, especially foreigners,\par sell the yen to hedge their stock positions, so the Japanese\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tends to rise when equities fall.\par     Still, the yen's outlook remains dark and other emerging\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are unlikely to extend gains, traders and\par analysts said.\par     "Dollar/yen is seen easily heading to 120, given the\par increased chances of a snap election and a delay in the sales\par tax hike," said Yuna Park, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bond analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dongbu\par Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Seoul.\par     "That will hurt other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , especially the won\par and the Taiwan dollar."\par     \par     WON\par     Tracking the yen's initial weakness, the won started the day\par by easing to 1,104.5 per dollar, its weakest since Sept. 2 2013.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  subsequently turned higher on the\par yen's rebound. Domestic exporters bought the won for settlements\par as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has chart support at 1,104.3 per dollar, the\par 61.8 percent Fibonacci retracement of its appreciation between\par June 2013 and July 2014.\par     Still, traders were wary of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South\par Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to check the won's\par  strength against the yen, traders said.\par     Earlier, the won rose as much as 0.7 percent to 9.3986\par against the Japanese unit, its strongest since August 2008.\par     A weakening yen raises concern that South Korea would lose\par competitiveness against Japan as the two countries compete to\par export a similar range of products, notably cars and electronic\par goods.\par     \par     \par     BAHT\par     The baht gained as Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Saturday\par the military government should use revenue and spending tools to\par stimulate the economy before turning to monetary policy.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  investors focused more on the dollar's broad\par weakness, as the yen rallied, than on disappointing Thai\par economic data.\par     Thailand's economy grew a much less-than-expected 1.1\par percent in the July-September period from the previous three\par months, the planning agency said.\par     The agency also trimmed its economic growth forecast for\par this year to 1.0 percent from 1.5-2.0 percent due to weak\par exports. \par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0435 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       115.71         116.25       +0.47\par   Sing dlr        1.2950         1.2975       +0.19\par   Taiwan dlr      30.670         30.766       +0.31\par   Korean won     1094.00        1100.50       +0.59\par   Baht             32.78          32.86       +0.26\par   Peso             44.88          44.94       +0.14\par   Rupiah        12188.00       12210.00       +0.18\par   Rupee            61.71          61.72       +0.02\par   Ringgit         3.3440         3.3470       +0.09\par   Yuan            6.1263         6.1307       +0.07\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       115.71         105.28       -9.02\par   Sing dlr        1.2950         1.2632       -2.46\par   Taiwan dlr      30.670         29.950       -2.35\par   Korean won     1094.00        1055.40       -3.53\par   Baht             32.78          32.86       +0.26\par   Peso             44.88          