\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Ringgit down despite solid output data, won leads Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  weaker\b0\par\par\uc2 648 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2014\par 05:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Malaysia Sept factory output better than expected\par     * Ringgit falls on lower oil prices worries\par     * Won slides on weaker yen, c.bank caution\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 11 (Reuters) - The Malaysian ringgit slid on\par Tuesday despite stronger-than-expected factory output data as\par most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  retreated as the dollar recovered\par its post-payrolls losses.\par     The won underperformed regional units as\par increased caution over potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the South\par Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to check its strength\par against a weak yen . The won also came under\par pressure versus the dollar ahead of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy\par meeting this week.\par     Malaysia's industrial production in September\par rose 5.4 percent from a year earlier, beating market\par expectations. \par     The data failed to support the ringgit as the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower oil prices dampened sentiment toward Malaysia,\par due to its status as a net oil exporter and major palm oil\par producer.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened in non-deliverable forwards (NDFs)\par  markets, with selling overnight by real money funds\par and reserve managers, traders said.\par     "Dips in one-month USD/MYR below 3.3400 are likely to remain\par well supported. Risk of a break through 3.3500 on spot can't be\par ruled out," said Jonathan Cavenagh, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Singapore.\par     The one-month ringgit NDFs eased 0.1 percent\par to 3.3521 per dollar, while spot ringgit fell 0.4 percent to\par 3.3430.\par     The dollar index, a gauge of its performance against\par six major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , steadied after recouping some of its\par post-payrolls losses.\par     \par     WON\par     The won slid against the dollar as offshore funds sold the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will hold a policy meeting on on\par Thursday with some expectations that interest rates could be cut\par by the year end.\par     Last month, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  unexpectedly eased monetary\par policy, driving the yen to a seven-year low. That darkened the\par outlook for Asia's fourth-largest economy as South Korean and\par Japanese companies compete for a similar group of products such\par as cars on major markets around the world.\par     "We now have an out-of-consensus call, expecting a 25bp rate\par cut to 1.75 percent in December and again to a new all-time low\par of 1.50 percent in Q1 2015, in an effort to limit downside risks\par to the economy," said Nomura economist Young Sun Kwon wrote in a\par research note.\par     "\f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  should not directly respond to a weaker\par JPY, but we firmly believe it will respond to weaker growth and\par lower inflation," Kwon added.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0430 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       115.08         114.87       -0.18\par   Sing dlr        1.2913         1.2910       -0.02\par   Taiwan dlr      30.531         30.606       +0.25\par   Korean won     1089.70        1085.00       -0.43\par   Baht             32.83          32.79       -0.12\par   Peso             44.92          44.86       -0.13\par   Rupiah        12170.00       12150.00       -0.16\par   Rupee            61.53          61.50       -0.06\par   Ringgit         3.3430         3.3305       -0.37\par   Yuan            6.1199         6.1196       -0.00\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       115.08         105.28       -8.52\par   Sing dlr        1.2913         1.2632       -2.18\par   Taiwan dlr      30.531         29.950       -1.90\par   Korean won     1089.70        1055.40       -3.15\par   Baht             32.83          32.86       +0.11\par   Peso             44.92          44.40       -1.17\par   Rupiah        12170.00       12160.00       -0.08\par   Rupee            61.53          61.80       +0.43\par   Ringgit         3.3430         3.2755       -2.02\par   Yuan            6.1199         6.0539       -1.08\par     \par \par  (Additional reporting by IFR Markets' Catherine Tan; Editing by\par SImon Cameron-Moore)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-11-11T05:56:25.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141111eabb004mr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
