\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah slides on impatience over fuel subsidy cuts; Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  firm\b0\par\par\uc2 684 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2014\par 06:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Fuel price not discussed in first cabinet meeting\par     * Importers, leveraged funds sell rupiah\par     * Won gains on exporters; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution limits\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Oct 28 (Reuters) - Indonesia's rupiah slipped to\par its lowest level in more than a week on investor impatience over\par planned fuel price hikes, as concerns grow that dithering by\par Jakarta to tackle its costly fuel subsidies could trigger\par capital outflows.\par     Most other emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  edged up, led by the\par South Korean won, as weak U.S. data tugged Treasury\par yields lower and dented the dollar against a basket of\par six-major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Indonesian President Joko Widodo on Monday held his first\par cabinet meeting, but cuts in fuel subsidies - top agenda for\par investors - were not discussed. \par     The rupiah lost as much as 0.5 percent to 12,170 on\par the greenback, its weakest since Oct. 17, on dollar demand from\par importers and leveraged funds.\par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate (JISDOR),\par which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  launched last year in an effort to manage\par exchange rate fluctuations, was fixed at 12,158 rupiah per\par dollar, weaker than Monday's 12,042.\par     "We have seen the initial euphoria on the political front\par quickly succumbed to the economic reality," said Andy Ji, Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  in\par Singapore.\par     The Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit a near four-week high on Oct. 21\par as reform-minded Widodo took office.\par     "Buy (dollar/rupiah) on dips remains our strategy for the\par next six months," said Ji. The rupiah could weaken past 12,500\par in the second quarter of the next year on expectations of higher\par U.S. interest rates, he added.\par     The U.S. Federal Reserve kicks off a two-day meeting later\par in the day and is all but certain to end its bond-buying\par program. \par     Last year, the rupiah was the worst-performing emerging\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with a 21 percent loss against the dollar,\par Thomson Reuters data showed.\par     Indonesia's dependence on foreign capital to fund its\par current account deficit has been a particular concern for\par markets, with the fuel subsides exacerbating the shortfall.\par     Widodo plans to order the steepest rise in subsidised fuel\par prices in nine years soon after he takes office, an advisor told\par Reuters earlier this month. \par     \par     WON\par     The won rose as much as 0.3 percent to 1,049.6 per dollar,\par its strongest since Sept. 29, on demand from exporters for\par month-end settlements.\par     Against the yen, the won advanced to 9.7256,\par its strongest since Oct. 6.\par     That heightened caution over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South\par Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to stem the won's strength.\par     South Korean and Japanese companies compete head-on for a\par similar group of products on major markets around the world.\par         \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0430 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       107.84         107.82       -0.02\par   Sing dlr        1.2738         1.2743       +0.04\par   Taiwan dlr      30.390         30.403       +0.04\par   Korean won     1049.90        1052.20       +0.22\par   Baht             32.42          32.45       +0.08\par   Peso             44.78          44.80       +0.04\par   Rupiah        12160.00       12110.00       -0.41\par   Rupee            61.38          61.30       -0.13\par   Ringgit         3.2760         3.2765       +0.02\par   Yuan            6.1135         6.1167       +0.05\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       107.84         105.28       -2.38\par   Sing dlr        1.2738         1.2632       -0.83\par   Taiwan dlr      30.390         29.950       -1.45\par   Korean won     1049.90        1055.40       +0.52\par   Baht             32.42          32.86       +1.35\par   Peso             44.78          44.40       -0.86\par   Rupiah        12160.00       12160.00       +0.00\par   Rupee            61.38          61.80       +0.68\par   Ringgit         3.2760         3.2755       -0.02\par   Yuan            6.1135         6.0539       -0.97\par     \par \par  (Additional reporting by Reuters \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Analyst Rick Lloyd; Editing\par by Shri Navaratnam)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-10-28T06:11:12.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141028eaas00590\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
