\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Relief over China's growth lifts Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; rupiah at 4-week high\b0\par\par\uc2 723 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2014\par 07:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Rupiah up on foreign banks' buying; Indonesian yields down\par     * Won may strengthen to 1,050.5/dollar - analysts\par     * Ringgit up on demand from offshore funds; importers limit\par gains\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Oct 21 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose\par on Tuesday as China's economic growth was stronger than expected\par in the third quarter, with the Indonesian rupiah hitting its\par highest in nearly four weeks on hopes a new government will push\par through economic reform.\par     China's economy, the world's second-largest, expanded 7.3\par percent in the third quarter from a year earlier. \par     That was slightly above the 7.2 percent forecast in a\par Reuters poll but the slowest pace since the 2008/09 global\par financial crisis, so some analysts still expect that Beijing\par will need to unveil more stimulus to support the economy.\par     "The data was positive for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the Chinese\par number was not that bad and we also have stimulus hopes," said\par Yuna Park, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bond analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dongbu Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  in\par Seoul.\par     She said she preferred the Chinese yuan, Thai\par baht and Indian rupee to other Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  due to stable inflation and politics.\par     The baht is the best-performing emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so\par far this year with a 2.0 percent appreciation against the\par dollar, according to Thomson Reuters data. The rupee was third\par best. \par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah rose as much as 0.7 percent to 11,950\par per dollar, its strongest since Sept. 25, on demand from foreign\par banks.\par     Government bond yields extended their slide, with the\par 10-year yield down to 8.035 percent, the lowest\par since Sept. 8.\par     "There are big expectations of the new leader," said a\par Jakarta-based \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader, referring to President Joko\par Widodo, who took office on Monday.\par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate (JISDOR),\par which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  launched last year in an effort to manage\par exchange rate fluctuations, was fixed at 11,993 rupiah per\par dollar, stronger than Monday's 12,041.\par     \par     WON\par     The South Korean won gained as the\par higher-than-expected Chinese growth data eased worries about the\par health of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's top export market.\par     Concern over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities weakened as the yen rose. \par     The won may strengthen further due to expectations of demand\par from exporters for month-end settlements, traders said.\par     "It is more likely to see the low 1,050 levels," said a\par South Korean bank trader in Seoul, referring to the won's\par exchange rate per dollar.\par     It may head to 1,050.5, the 38.2 percent Fibonacci\par retracement of its depreciation between September and October.\par     It was around 1,053 per dollar on Tuesday.\par \par     RINGGIT\par     Malaysia's ringgit gained as offshore real money\par funds bought its non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) to\par seek higher yields, traders said.\par     But spot ringgit pared some of its gains as traders took\par profits. Dollar demand from local importers was also cited.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0430 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       106.46         106.95       +0.46\par   Sing dlr        1.2680         1.2695       +0.12\par   Taiwan dlr      30.379         30.415       +0.12\par   Korean won     1053.41        1059.60       +0.59\par   Baht             32.23          32.32       +0.29\par   Peso             44.77          44.82       +0.12\par   Rupiah        11985.00       12030.00       +0.38\par   Rupee            61.27          61.36       +0.15\par   Ringgit         3.2565         3.2720       +0.48\par   Yuan            6.1217         6.1229       +0.02\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       106.46         105.28       -1.11\par   Sing dlr        1.2680         1.2632       -0.38\par   Taiwan dlr      30.379         29.950       -1.41\par   Korean won     1053.41        1055.40       +0.19\par   Baht             32.23          32.86       +1.96\par   Peso             44.77          44.40       -0.83\par   Rupiah        11985.00       12160.00       +1.46\par   Rupee            61.27          61.80       +0.87\par   Ringgit         3.2565         3.2755       +0.58\par   Yuan            6.1217         6.0539       -1.11\par     \par \par  (Additional reporting by KyoungHo Lee in Seoul; Editing by Alan\par Raybould)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-10-21T06:14:45.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA00000201