\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Slips as Stocks Rally -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,812 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 2014\par 03:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.1195-6.1272    6.1000-6.1350 \par USD/TWD   30.370-30.440    30.300-30.500 \par USD/KRW    1,060-1,068      1,057-1,070 \par USD/SGD   1.2733-1.2765    1.2705-1.2795 \par USD/MYR   3.2620-3.2740    3.2500-3.2870 \par USD/THB    32.31-32.42      32.20-32.53 \par USD/PHP    44.74-44.90      44.58-45.00 \par USD/IDR   12,040-12,130    12,00-12,230 \par USD/INR    61.10-61.37      61.00-62.63 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--downtrend. A return of risk appetite for U.S. stocks on Friday could lift investor sentiment in Asia and help emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally. The bearish technical bias for spot USD/CNY - implying more yuan gains are likely - will remain in play if the ceiling of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at 6.1272 is intact by Monday's close. Spot USD/CNY could chalk up a fresh 7-month low if it surpasses Thursday's 6.1209. The yuan is still "significantly undervalued" despite recent appreciation, said the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  department last week, while also chastising aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \uc2 HSBC China\uc2  flash manufacturing PMI for October due Thursday will be the week's data highlight. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.1195 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.1000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 6.1272 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1350 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 6.1427 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation. USD/TWD is likely to drift between the consolidation zone formed by the lower and upper Bollinger bands (standard deviation 1) which span 30.300-30.440. The U.S. dollar index inched higher overnight as the yield on the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury bill rose to 2.20%. But the rebound of U.S. equities could help boost risk appetite in Asia and thus mitigate the possible effect of a stronger U.S. dollar due to the rebound in U.S. yields. A risk rally could see the price of the USD/TWD 1-month nondeliverable forward contract - which is a gauge of speculative sentiment - fall further below that of the spot contract. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.370 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 30.300 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 30.220 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.440 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.500 (psychological trading barrier), before 30.510 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation. USD/KRW is likely to hover within a consolidation range of 1,057-1,068. The U.S. dollar index is stabilising at lower levels versus Friday's close due to risk appetite returning, but the rebound of \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields could keep the dollar afloat. The U.S. 10-year government bond yield has bounced back to 2.20% from around 2.00% on Friday. If USD/KRW climbs above 1,068, the daily Bollinger uptrend channel will come back into effect and fuel bullish USD/KRW bets. Data released Monday showed a 0.4% annual drop in producer prices in September versus the 0.2% fall registered in August - which may justify \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2 's recent interest rate cut to boost the economy. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,060 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1,059 (base of weekly Ichimoku Cloud support zone), then at 1,057 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 1,068 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,070 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation. USD/SGD is currently in a narrow range between the lower and upper Bollinger bands (standard deviation 1) but could inch higher as the U.S. dollar index appears to have bottomed out for now. If USD/SGD ends the day above 1.2765 it would be inside the daily as well as weekly Bollinger uptrend channel - suggesting more greenback strength to come in the near-to-medium term. The dollar is finding support from the rebound in the yield of the benchmark 10-year \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  bill to 2.2%. Looking ahead, traders are focusing on China's October \uc2 HSBC\uc2  flash manufacturing PMI data due Thursday for the next volatility catalyst. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2733 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 1.2705 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2700 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 1.2765 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2795 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2800 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--uptrend may end. USD/MYR is slipping out of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel as the return of risk appetite depresses the U.S. dollar in Asia. On Friday, U.S. stocks rose - translating to higher equity markets in Asia early Monday. The ringgit has rebounded to 3.2685 from its Friday close of 3.2740 thus breaking the base of the Bollinger uptrend channel. A Monday close below 3.2740 could motivate U.S. dollar selling toward the Bollinger downtrend channel at 3.2490. Malaysia's September consumer price index published on Friday revealed a slowing inflation rate - which is likely temporary due to the fuel price hikes not factoring in yet. A slower rise in inflation could theoretically delay the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's next interest rate increase. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2620 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 3.2500 (round-figure trading barrier), before 3.2490 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.2740 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2870 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.3000 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--possible downtrend. USD/THB has slid to the 32.31 entrance of the Bollinger downtrend channel as risk appetite makes a gradual return. Confirmation of the downtrend channel coming into effect could send the baht toward 32.12 where the USD/THB Ichimoku Cloud support awaits. The Thai baht, along with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is slightly stronger following the rebound of U.S. stocks on Friday which has eased fears of a prolonged equity meltdown. But if USD/THB ends Monday above 32.31, technical consolidation could dominate for the near term. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.31 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 32.20 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 32.12 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 32.42 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 32.53 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 32.64 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation lower. As general risk appetite returns, USD/PHP is likely to drop out of the Bollinger uptrend channel - which had been supporting at 44.90 - and fall to the 20-day Bollinger mid line at 44.74. A rebound in U.S. stocks on Friday has triggered a rally in early Asian equity markets Monday. If the improving sentiment carries on for the rest of the week, USD/PHP could test the entrance to the Bollinger downtrend channel at 44.58. The \uc2 Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meets on Thursday to review its monetary policy. Recent tepid Philippine inflation data has dampened the chances of a peso-positive interest rate hike. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.74 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 44.58 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 44.56 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.90 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 45.00 (round-figure trading barrier), before 45.05 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--consolidation lower. The collapse of USD/IDR on Friday - following a surprising show of support for president-elect Joko Widodo by some of his keenest rivals - is likely to trigger more short-term downside for the dollar. The inauguration of Mr. Widodo Monday could add to rising investor sentiment - which had been feeble in late September due to signs of political opposition to Mr. Widodo's plans for reform. The return of risk appetite in global markets on Friday could also help weigh USD/IDR toward the Bollinger downtrend channel that begins at 12,040. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 12,040 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 12,000 (round-figure trading barrier), before 11,940 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 12,130 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 12,230 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 12,270 (year high).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation lower. USD/INR may fall to the Bollinger downtrend channel at 61.10 as risk appetite returns. A Monday close below 61.10 could trigger more U.S. dollar selling. The rebound of U.S. stocks has eased concerns of a deeper market correction, and thus helped Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to recoup losses. The rupee has also risen partly because of a local stock market rally triggered by the pro-business Bharatiya Janata Party winning local polls last week. But hedge funds - which according to a trader may have recently turned bearish on the rupee - may prop up USD/INR on dips. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 61.10 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 61.00 (round-figure trading barrier), before 60.84 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 61.37 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 61.63 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 61.91 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 19 Oct 2014 21:03 ET  USD/Asia Slips as Stocks Rally -- Asia Daily -2-\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 19, 2014 21:03 ET (01:03 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141020eaak00067\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
