\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Bouyant As U.S. Bond Yields Rebound -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,840 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 2014\par 03:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.1208-6.1282    6.1000-6.1355 \par USD/TWD   30.370-30.440    30.300-30.500 \par USD/KRW    1,059-1,060      1,054-1,067 \par USD/SGD   1.2730-1.2762    1.2705-1.2795 \par USD/MYR   3.2740-3.2870    3.2600-3.3000 \par USD/THB    32.30-32.41      32.18-32.53 \par USD/PHP    44.70-44.89      44.52-45.00 \par USD/IDR   12,230-12,270    12,130-12,340 \par USD/INR    61.66-61.95      61.37-62.50 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--downtrend. The bearish technical bias for spot USD/CNY continues, reinforced by the ceiling of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at 6.1282. Spot USD/CNY could chalk up a fresh 7-month low if it surpasses Thursday's 6.1209. The yuan is still "significantly undervalued" despite recent appreciation, said the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  department on Thursday, while also chastising aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Overnight, risk aversion was soothed by signs of improving industrial production in the U.S., which could translate to a mild risk rally in Asia. \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  bonds pared recent gains, propping up the yield on the benchmark 10-year \uc2 Treasury\uc2  bill back above 2.0% - which helped the U.S. dollar stabilize. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.1208 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.1000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 6.1282 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1355 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 6.1428 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation. USD/TWD may linger above the 20-day Bollinger mid support line at 30.370 as the U.S. dollar index stabilized overnight. Asia likely sees a respite from risk aversion as U.S. stocks ended flat on a rise in U.S. industrial production for September and weekly U.S. jobless claims falling to a 14-year low. While the return of risk appetite could buoy emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rebound of the yield on the benchmark U.S. 10-year \uc2 Treasury\uc2  bond could keep the greenback supported. A relief rally for risk assets could see the discount between the price of the USD/TWD 1-month nondeliverable forward contract and that of the spot contract increase. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.370 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 30.300 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 30.230 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.440 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.500 (psychological trading barrier), before 30.510 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation. USD/KRW will likely hover within a consolidation range of 1,055-1,066 as markets take a breather from risk aversion and the U.S. 10-year government bond yield resurfaces above 2.0%, providing support to the greenback. If the U.S. dollar climbs above 1,066, the daily Bollinger uptrend channel will come back into effect and potentially fuel bullish USD/KRW bets. The recent trend of investors buying bonds while selling stocks and the U.S. dollar dissipated overnight on a gain in U.S. industrial production in September and jobless claims falling to a 14-year low. Heading into the weekend, there could be a relief rally for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors cut back on bearish positions. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,059 (base of weekly Ichimoku Cloud support zone), then at 1,054 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 1,050 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 1,060 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1,067 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,070 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation. USD/SGD is currently in a narrow range between the lower and upper Bollinger bands (standard deviation 1) but could inch higher as the U.S. dollar index appears to have bottomed out for now. If USD/SGD ends Friday above 1.2763 it would be inside the daily as well as weekly Bollinger uptrend channel--suggesting more greenback strength to come in the near-to-medium term. The dollar is finding support from the overnight rise in the yield of the benchmark 10-year \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  note. The U.S. stock market selloff appears to have eased following strong U.S. industrial production data in September and another drop in unemployment claims. This could check the bleeding of equity markets in Asia that began early October. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2730 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 1.2705 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2700 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 1.2762 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2795 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2800 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--uptrend continues. USD/MYR is still creeping higher inside the daily Bollinger uptrend channel, helped by a firmness seen in the U.S. dollar index overnight. The rebound in the yield of the benchmark 10-year \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  bill above 2.0% may have lifted the greenback. If USD/MYR stays above 3.2740 by the end of Friday the likelihood of more gains next week will increase. The ringgit could then fall past September's 6-month low of 3.2860 to the U.S. dollar. Malaysia will publish its September consumer price index at 0901 GMT. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2740 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2600 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 3.2500 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 3.2870 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.3000 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation. USD/THB likely remains stuck near the 20-day Bollinger mid line at 32.40 as the benchmark ICE U.S. dollar index stabilized overnight. A likely consolidation range for USD/THB in the near term is 32.30-32.53. The pair has been relatively less volatile compared to its peers over the past week, partly because domestic leads have been lacking. Overnight, risk aversion toned down after an improvement was seen in U.S. industrial production--which lifted stocks and weighed on bonds. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.30 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 32.18 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 32.41 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 32.53 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 32.64 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation lower. USD/PHP may continue to shy away from the Bollinger uptrend channel as risk appetite makes a timid recovery. Asian stocks might get a reprieve from the recent sharp selloffs after U.S. markets overnight managed to eke out marginal gains on improving U.S. industrial production data. A relief rally for emerging markets could see USD/PHP slip back down below the 20-day Bollinger mid support at 44.70. Last week, Philippine inflation data showed prices rose less than in August, dampening the chances of a Oct. 23 interest rate hike--which could have positive connotations for the peso. The \uc2 Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meets next week to review its monetary policy. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.70 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 44.52 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support and daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.89 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 45.00 (round-figure trading barrier), before 45.08 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--consolidation higher. USD/IDR is likely to stay elevated within its daily Bollinger uptrend channel as the yield on the benchmark 10-year \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  note rose back above 2.0%, providing a base for the recently battered U.S. dollar. The U.S. dollar has recently been tracking the moves of \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  bonds closely as traders get spooked by the sharp fall in bond yields--which makes it less appealing to hold the greenback. A Thursday uptick in U.S. industrial production lowered demand for safe haven bonds and helped stocks to claw back from losses and end the day in the black. But USD/IDR may still find buyers on dips due to the possibility of economic and structural reform being delayed. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 12,230 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 12,130 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 12,000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 12,270 (year high), then at 12,340 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 12,500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--uptrend. The rupee fell sharply Thursday, possibly due to state-owned banks buying the U.S. dollar for energy funding needs. The USD/INR pair has thus entered the Bollinger uptrend channel, suggesting more gains ahead are likely. The bullish technical bias will be affirmed on a Friday close above 61.66--the base of the uptrend channel. Adding to support for the U.S. dollar was the overnight rise of the yield on the benchmark U.S. 10-year \uc2 Treasury\uc2  note from its 16-month low notched mid-week. The recent steep fall in oil prices--which ought to buffer India's current account deficit - is however a bearish signal for the world economy that in turn might have repercussions for India's economy. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 61.66 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 61.37 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 61.08 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 61.95 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 62.00 (round-figure trading barrier), before 62.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 16 Oct 2014 21:02 ET  USD/Asia Bouyant As U.S. Bond Yields Rebound -- -2-\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 16, 2014 21:02 ET (01:02 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141017eaah0003u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
