\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-U.S. warns Europe on deflation, says ECB actions may fall short\b0\par\par\uc2 526 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2014\par 23:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Obama administration wants Germany to increase demand\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  taken to task for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has eased but yuan still undervalued (Adds comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 , China, paragraphs 5-13)\par \par \uc2 By Jason Lange\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, Oct 15 (Reuters) - The United States on Wednesday renewed a warning that Europe risks falling into a downward spiral of falling wages and prices, saying recent actions by the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not be enough to ward off deflation.\par \par \uc2 In a semiannual report to Congress, the \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2  also said Berlin could do more to help Europe, namely by boosting demand in the German economy, Europe's largest.\par \par \uc2 "Europe faces the risk of a prolonged period of substantially below-target inflation or outright deflation," the Treasury said.\par \par \uc2 The ECB in recent months has cut interest rates to record lows, offered banks new long-term loans, and announced plans to buy private sector assets.\par \par \uc2 All this is intended to prop up a euro zone economy teetering on the edge of recession. Europe is a major trading partner for the United States and China, and its travails have been at the center of worries over the global economy that have shaken financial markets worldwide in recent days.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  said the ECB's actions "should help combat deflationary risks," but that "further policy support for demand may be needed."\par \par \uc2 The report appeared carefully worded to avoid sounding pushy over what Washington thinks Germany should do. Berlin has been a key American ally for decades.\par \par \uc2 Still, the Obama administration sees Germany as a missing link in Europe's elusive recovery from what in many corners of the continent has looked like an economic depression.\par \par \uc2 "Measures to increase domestic demand, particularly in surplus countries like Germany, can help further European and global rebalancing," the Treasury said. In its last report to Congress in April, it had also warned that Europe faced the risk of deflation.\par \par \uc2 Germany, which has sought to keep the focus in Europe on fiscal austerity, came under a spotlight at meetings last weekend of finance officials from around the globe who sought to convince Berlin to loosen its purse strings.\par \par \uc2 The Treasury Department also took \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  to task for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. The won has weakened 5 percent against the dollar in six weeks.\par \par \uc2 The Obama administration has long called on Seoul to minimize \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but on Wednesday it said outright that the won was "undervalued," and urged Seoul to let it appreciate further.\par \par \uc2 Washington again called China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "significantly undervalued," but said Beijing appeared to be taking less of a hand in determining the yuan's value. This suggests tensions between the two powers over \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy might be easing.\par \par \uc2 The semiannual report examines the economic and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies of major U.S. trading partners. It did not formally label any country a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator, and has not done so in any report since 1994. (Reporting by Jason Lange; editing by Cynthia Osterman, Leslie Adler and David Gregorio) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-10-15T22:54:36.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141015eaaf00oe4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
