\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Philippine peso leads Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  losses after weak imports\b0\par\par\uc2 715 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2014\par 07:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Philippine July electronics imports drop most in 2 years\par     * Won down; offshore funds sell on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution\par     * Won turns weaker vs yen after six-year high\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 25 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso hit a\par five-month low on Thursday, leading weakness among emerging\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as the dollar hit a four-year high against\par major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with the euro slumping.\par     The peso underperformed its regional peers after\par the country's July electronics imports reported the steepest\par drop in more than two years, indicating an economic slowdown.\par  \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's won fell on growing caution over\par possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to\par curb its strength against the yen. The South Korean\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier hit a six-year peak to the Japanese unit.\par     The dollar index, a gauge of the greenback's\par performance against a six major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , rose to its highest\par since July 2010.\par     That came as the euro fell to a 14-month low versus\par the dollar as European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mario Draghi\f28 \uc2 \f2  said\par on Wednesday monetary policy will be kept loose for as long as\par it takes to push ultra-low inflation back up towards the two\par percent level. \par     "It is more difficult for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to strengthen\par against a firm USD," said Frances Cheung, head of Asian rates\par strategy at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Agricole\f28 \uc2 \f2  CIB in Hong Kong.\par     Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have benefitted from expectations\par that investors would borrow cheap euros to buy higher-yielding\par assets in the region.\par     But, Cheung said that while easier monetary policies by the\par ECB and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  may limit losses in emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the impact may not be as supportive on the regional\par units as initially hoped.\par     Money from the ECB may focus more on buying peripheral bonds\par or domestic bank loans, while Japanese investors do not like to\par buy other Asian assets, Cheung said. Japan's investors prefer\par safer assets such as U.S. Treasuries.\par     "We have to be conservative at first (on emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 )," she added.\par         \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par     The peso lost as much as 0.5 percent to 44.675 per dollar,\par its weakest since April 25.\par     Philippine electronics imports in July fell nearly 30\par percent from a year earlier, the steepest drop since March 2012,\par data showed earlier.\par     That indicates weaker electronics exports going forward as\par most imports products are raw materials to produce electronics\par shipments.\par     The peso is likely to stay under pressure from the dollar's\par broad strength, traders said.\par     "I'd still want to buy the dollar/peso on dips," said a\par senior Philippine trader in Manila, adding he would buy the pair\par for a target of 44.70.\par         \par     WON\par     The won eased again on selling from offshore funds and its\par weakness in non-deliverable forwards markets.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pared initial losses thanks to \par demand from exporters for month-end settlements.\par     The won turned weaker against the yen after strengthening to\par 9.5069, its strongest since August 2008.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0415 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       109.11         109.04       -0.06\par   Sing dlr        1.2674         1.2668       -0.05\par   Taiwan dlr      30.274         30.248       -0.09\par   Korean won     1042.70        1039.90       -0.27\par   Baht             32.24          32.22       -0.06\par   Peso             44.65          44.46       -0.43\par   Rupiah        11950.00       11950.00       +0.00\par   Rupee            61.01          60.96       -0.07\par   Ringgit         3.2450         3.2425       -0.08\par   Yuan            6.1356         6.1346       -0.02\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       109.11         105.28       -3.51\par   Sing dlr        1.2674         1.2632       -0.33\par   Taiwan dlr      30.274         29.950       -1.07\par   Korean won     1042.70        1055.40       +1.22\par   Baht             32.24          32.86       +1.92\par   Peso             44.65          44.40       -0.57\par   Rupiah        11950.00       12160.00       +1.76\par   Rupee            61.01          61.80       +1.30\par   Ringgit   