\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Fed rate view hurts Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; ringgit hits 4-mth low before c.bank meets\b0\par\par\uc2 516 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2014\par 10:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Updates prices. For midday report, double-click\par  )\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 18 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par slid on Thursday as the U.S. Federal Reserve's outlook for\par rising rates stoked concerns that regional assets may lose some\par of their high-yield appeal.\par     The Malaysian ringgit fell to its weakest in more\par than four months ahead of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy\par review later in the day. Economists were evenly split between\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara\f28 \uc2 \f2  raising interest rates again and holding steady.\par  \par     South Korea's won ended local trade down 0.8\par percent at 1,043.4 per dollar, its weakest since April 16.\par     Offshore funds sold the won on expectations that the yen's\par weakness will hurt South Korean companies' competitiveness\par against Japanese rivals. The yen hit a six-year low\par against the dollar.\par     The won eased against the yen after hitting a\par six-year peak on caution over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South\par Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities.\par     Indonesia's rupiah slid to a near three-month low\par versus the dollar, losing as much as 0.7 percent to 12,035 per\par dollar. It was the first time the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  breached the\par 12,000-level since June 30. \par     The rupiah later pared losses on apparent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and as the new government\par plans to raise the price of subsidised fuel. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  earlier introduced a set of new rules on\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading to encourage more derivative trading\par and deepen the market. \par     Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  later recovered some of their\par losses as the dollar eased against a basket of major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Wednesday suggested it could raise interest rates\par faster than expected when it starts increasing, although it\par renewed its pledge to keep borrowing costs near zero for a\par "considerable time." \par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0800 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       108.54         108.37       -0.16\par   Sing dlr        1.2665         1.2674       +0.07\par   Taiwan dlr      30.250         30.134       -0.38\par   Korean won     1043.10        1034.90       -0.79\par   Baht             32.26          32.23       -0.09\par   Peso             44.42          44.26       -0.36\par   Rupiah        11990.00       11950.00       -0.33\par   Rupee            60.94          60.92       -0.02\par   Ringgit         3.2275         3.2175       -0.31\par   Yuan            6.1442         6.1401       -0.07\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 