\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Fed, China policy speculation bolster Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 495 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2014\par 09:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Updates prices. For midday report, double-click\par  )\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 17 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose on Wednesday helped by doubt over the timing of\par a U.S. interest rate rise and on media reports saying \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is providing liquidity to support the economy.\par     Regional units pared some of their earlier gains with the\par dollar broadly firm as investors awaited the U.S. Federal\par Reserve's latest guidance on interest rates later in the day.\par     Worries about an earlier-than-expected rate hike by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par eased after the Wall Street Journal's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  watcher said the U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may keep the words "considerable time" in its\par policy statement after the Tuesday-Wednesday meeting.\par     Malaysia's ringgit gained as investors covered\par short positions ahead of inflation data later in the day. The\par country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is also set to review monetary policy on\par Thursday, with economists divided on a further rate hike.\par  \par     The South Korean won ended local trade higher\par against the dollar amid market talk of demand from a major U.S.\par asset management company for two-year monetary stabilisation\par bonds.\par     Against the yen, the won hit a six-year high.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were suspected of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the won's strength, traders said.\par     Indonesian's rupiah edged up as Jakarta shares\par  rose 1.2 percent, far outperforming Southeast Asian\par peers.\par     The Thai baht showed little reaction after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank\par of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  left interest rates unchanged, as widely expected.\par  \par     The Singapore dollar bucked the regional\par appreciation trend despite stronger-than-expected August exports\par data as shipments to major economies slowed. \par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par                                                            \par   Change on the day at   0724 GMT                          \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       107.25         107.12       -0.12\par   Sing dlr        1.2620         1.2601       -0.15\par   Taiwan dlr      30.123         30.160       +0.12\par   Korean won     1034.20        1036.70       +0.24\par   Baht             32.21          32.24       +0.09\par   Peso             44.14          44.23       +0.20\par   Rupiah        11935.00       11960.00       +0.21\par   Rupee            60.96          61.06       +0.15\par   Ringgit         3.2150         3.2290       +0.44\par   Yuan            6.1412         6.1462       +0.08\par                                                            \par   Change so far in 2014                                    \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       107.25         105.28       -1.84\par   Sing dlr        1.2620         1.2632       +0.10\par   Taiwan dlr      30.123         29.950       -0.57\par   Korean wo