\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea June  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves rise on bond issuance,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2014\par 23:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SEOUL, July 3 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's foreign reserves in\par June rose by the biggest amount in eight months to a new record\par high, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data showed on Thursday, after the country\par issued bonds denominated in U.S. dollars and euros last month.\par     Foreign reserves stood at $366.55 billion at the end of\par June, \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a statement, up $5.63 billion\par from the previous month in the reserves' biggest monthly gain\par since October 2013.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  attributed the gain mainly to the\par government's decision early in June to sell $2 billion of dollar\par and euro bonds as it aimed to set a fresh benchmark for other\par domestic debt issuers. \par     It also said the reserves rose on management gains and after\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the euro gained in value against the\par dollar. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  does not provide breakdowns of its\par reserves.\par     June's gain comes after market participants suspected\par dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to\par water down the Korean won's rise against the greenback,\par which frequently raises concerns it could undermine local\par exporters' profits.\par     A \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  official refused to confirm whether the\par reserves had risen from direct market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The won firmed 0.8 percent against the dollar in June, and\par is up 4.6 percent so far this year.\par     South Korea has the world's seventh largest reserves, 91.7\par percent of which are in the form of securities.\par     \par     South Korean foreign reserves (in $ bln, at end-month,\par rounded):\par  Jun     May     Apr     Mar     Feb     Jan      Dec\par  366.55  360.91  355.85  354.34  351.79  348.39   346.46\par \par  (Reporting by Christine Kim; Editing by Kim Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-7-2T22:00:03.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140702ea7200d4s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
