\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 South Korea \highlight\uc2  Won at 6-Year High,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Suspected -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2014\par 04:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0205 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The South Korea won notched a 6-year high of 1,009.3 to the U.S. dollar as risk appetite improved following overnight record highs on Wall Street. But USD/KRW is bouncing back to the round-figure trading barrier of 1,010 as traders take profit, suspecting that \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  may be supporting the dollar just under that mark. The implication of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 --as yet unconfirmed--is that the won will not be able to rally much more. The weekly chart however, does suggest there is more room for the dollar to fall, possibly to the bottom of the weekly Bollinger downtrend channel at 995--which is very close to the July 2008 low. USD/KRW is now 1,009.9 from its Tuesday close of 1,011.7. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0202 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  expects yields at both China and Malaysia airlines to recover in 2014 thanks to slower capacity growth. Yields are an important measurement of airline profitability. "Concern around fuel-price hikes detracts from the key theme of recovering yields in our opinion," it says. \uc2 Barclays\uc2 ' top pick of full-service airlines is China Southern (1055.HK) because of an attractive valuation and higher return on equity compared with its international competitors. It keeps an Overweight rating on the stock with a target price of HK$4.11. \uc2 Barclays\uc2 ' top pick among low-cost carriers is \uc2 AirAsia Bhd\uc2 . (5099.KU) because yields in Malaysia's market will likely bottom out to its benefit. It maintains an Overweight rating with a target price of MYR3.00. (joanne.chiu@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0155 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Capital Economics predicts a bearish year for corn, soybeans and wheat following the latest quarterly stocks and crop progress reports from the \uc2 United States Department of Agriculture\uc2  Tuesday. "U.S. crop production could be extremely large this year, and easily exceed last year's." It tips the price of corn and soybeans to fall to $3.50/bushel and $10/bushel respectively, and wheat to drop to $5.00/bushel by the end of the year -- this assuming that there isn't a "repeat of the adverse weather seen in 2012." July corn futures settled at a six-month low after release of the USDA report to $4.22 3/4 a bushel. July wheat futures closed at their lowest level since Jan. 31 of $5.59 3/4 a bushel, and July soybeans to $14.00 a bushel. (isabella.steger@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0153 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] USD/KRW falls to 1,010.0 from an opening of 1,011.8 but strong bids may be reinforcing the round-figure trading barrier of 1,010. The possibility that \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  might step in to defend that level may be motivating traders to trim their dollar-shorts, said one trader. If the 1,010 level is breached, there could be stop-loss orders activated that would push USD/KRW even lower. In addition, traders might read it as a sign that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is giving the green light for the won to rally further; this would encourage more speculative bets on the won that would add to downside pressure on USD/KRW. USD/KRW is now 1,010.1 from its Tuesday close of 1,011.7. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0144 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Taiwan shares hit another multiyear high on opening driven by strong foreign inflows into technology heavyweights. The index is up 0.5% to 9502.68. "The buying spree is mostly prompted by the stellar gains on Wall Street and we expect the uptrend to continue," a local trader says but adds some profit-taking may be seen mid-session as some players are taking precautions to avoid an overheated market. TSMC (2330.TW) is up 1.9% at NT$130, Hon Hai (2317.TW) gains 2.0% to tN$103.50, HTC (2498.TW) rises 1.1% atNT$139.50 and Largan (3008.TW) is up 2.8% at NT$2,390. The index is tipped to move between 9450 and 9520. (jenny.hsu@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0143 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The Australian dollar fell from 96.27 to as low as 96.08 against the yen after Australia's May trade deficit came in at A$1.91 billion, much wider than the A$100 million deficit consensus forecast. Further downside in AUD/JPY may encounter support at 95.97 and 95.64 on hourly charts. Spot AUD/JPY was last at 96.16. (jerry.tan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0142 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The Nikkei is up 0.6% at 15418.82--breaking through 15400 for the first time since June 23 and defying profit-taking after Tuesday's 1.1% rise. Volume is fairly strong. "Buying is consistent and continues to defy gyrations in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market where a sluggish dollar would normally invite selling," \uc2 Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp\uc2 . strategist Daisuke Uno says. "It's clear that the market has shifted from a focus on dollar/yen to a focus on fundamentals as well as expectations for still more buying ahead from public sources. As such it's difficult for investors who have traditionally powered the market--such as hedge funds--to participate as the downside fear has lessened." (bradford.frischkorn@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0141 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Don't assume the worst is over for Macau following that nearly 4% drop in gambling revenue last month, Union Gaming says in a note to clients. The gaming-focused research firm, which last month issued its first bearish call on the sector since 2011, estimates VIP revenue fell about 20% in June and will stay weak in the near-term. "We don't think that a prolonged weak VIP story is necessarily built into consensus at this point," Union says, pointing to recent conversations with investors that suggest consensus is for "flat-to-down" VIP revenue in the coming months. High-end gamblers are a big business for Macau, accounting for about two-thirds of the Chinese territory's $45 billion gambling industry. (mia.lamar@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0138 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Spot USD/CNY could activate a bearish technical signal if it ends Wednesday below the base of the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone at 6.2019. If the round-figure trading barrier at 6.2000 is also breached by day's end, the likelihood of further yuan appreciation versus the dollar will increase. The yuan has rallied four consecutive days, partly due to the U.S. dollar's broad decline, but has stalled Wednesday after an unexpectedly higher daily USD/CNY parity rate of 6.1549 versus Tuesday's 6.1523. Investor sentiment may be improving after Tuesday's upbeat China official manufacturing PMI for June, which rose to 51.0 from the previous month's 50.8, and could thus aid yuan gains. USD/CNY is now 6.2080 from its Monday close of 6.2016. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0125 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The ANZ Commodity Price Index recorded a fourth successive monthly decline in June easing 0.9% in the month to be 6.7% below its peak in February. "The headline index figure is now at its lowest level in 15 months but this masks divergent trends across the subgroups," \uc2 ANZ Bank\uc2  Economist Steve Edwards says. Dairy and forestry have fallen to 16- and 14-month lows, respectively, but some other prices are rising. Meat prices have risen to a 14.5 year high and seafood prices remain at a record, Edwards says. The NZD strengthened slightly in June exacerbating the fall in commodity prices once converted into local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he says. (rebecca.howard@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @FarroHoward)\par \par \uc2 0124 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The Australian dollar reached a two-week high of 1.0836 against its New Zealand counterpart Wednesday morning, stalling near the 55-day moving average, as it extends its Tuesday's gains following less-dovish-than-expected comments from the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2 . Further upside in spot AUD/NZD may encounter resistance at 1.0868 (50% Fibonacci retracement of 1.1034-1.0701 June 4 to June 26 decline), and then at 1.0907 (61.8% Fibonacci retracement which is just below the 200-day moving average). Spot AUD/NZD was last at 1.0821 as markets await Australia's May trade balance data due at 0130 GMT. (jerry.tan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0122 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Tocom rubber futures are higher due to China logging in positive June manufacturing data Tuesday and after the \uc2 Association of Natural Rubber Producing Countries\uc2  said H1 production only increased marginally due to low prices which discourages farmers from tapping. Traders say raw material supply has been tight and are not recovering as fast as previous years even as major producing regions enter the current peak output season. Benchmark December rubber trades Y2.2 higher at Y213.3/kg. (huileng.tan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 01, 2014 22:05 ET (02:05 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140702ea720004o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
