\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Mixed, China PMI Effect Fades -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,787 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2014\par 02:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par          Immediate Range   Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.2234-6.2318    6.2104-6.2364 \par USD/TWD   30.000-30.040    29.770-30.140 \par USD/KRW    1,018-1,020      1,015-1,023 \par USD/SGD   1.2412-1.2485    1.2400-1.2538 \par USD/MYR   3.2080-3.2180    3.1870-3.2280 \par USD/THB    32.37-32.45      32.22-32.53 \par USD/PHP    43.70-43.80      43.58-43.92 \par USD/IDR   11,920-12,000    11,810-12,200 \par USD/INR    60.00-60.46      59.54-60.84 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. Spot USD/CNY can be expected to linger around its recent level, lacking a catalyst from economic data or big moves in the U.S. dollar index. Monday's improved HSBC China flash manufacturing PMI data failed to give the yuan a boost although it helped equities halt the prior three-day loss. The daily USD/CNY parity rate will likely remain within the 6.1500-6.1600 range that has held for the past eight sessions, and will add to non-volatility in spot USD/CNY. But if spot USD/CNY closes above 6.2364, which would place it above the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and also above the 20-day Bollinger mid line, a bullish technical bias could form for the greenback. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.2234 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.2104 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.2000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 6.2318 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud), then at 3.2364 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 6.2494 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation. The supportive tone in USD/TWD continues as the pair again meets strong buying near the 30.000 round-figure trading barrier - suspected to be from the \uc2 Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On Monday, Taiwan's industrial output index hit a record high of 109.56 - a 5.19% on-year increase for May. The improvement reflects an increase in demand for consumer goods also seen in China's improved manufacturing PMI which was also released Monday. Continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been propping up the greenback and deterring bullish bets on the Taiwan dollar. In the offshore nondeliverable forward market, the pricing of the benchmark 1-month contract suggests a neutral to mildly bullish sentiment for the greenback. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.000 (round-figure trading barrier), before 29.770 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.040 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 30.090 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 30.140 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel and daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation. USD/KRW needs to break out of the 1,018-1,020 technical rut in order to gain some momentum. On a Tuesday close below 1,018, the daily Bollinger downtrend channel comes into effect and could exert a downward force toward the channel's base at 1,015. But if the 1,020 round-figure trading barrier - also the 20-day Bollinger mid line resistance - is breached, USD/KRW could take on a mild bullish bias. The market remains wary of \uc2 the Bank of Korea\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  won rises too fast - which was hinted at by authorities recently. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,018 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,015 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,010 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 1,020 (round-figure trading barrier and 20-day Bollinger mid), before 1,023 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--downside bias. If USD/SGD remains below 1.2485 by the end of the day, the daily Bollinger downtrend channel will remain in play and guide the greenback lower toward the daily chart support at 1.2412. Despite the slight rise in yield of the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury yield, which last traded at 2.63%, the greenback appears to be under mild pressure, possibly due to improved risk appetite following the upbeat HSBC China manufacturing PMI released on Monday. The Chinese data, which hit a 7-month high and signalled expansion of the sector, spurred risk appetite for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in general. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2412 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2400 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 1.2485 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1.2500 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1.2538 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--consolidation. USD/MYR is still trapped in a technical consolidate range spanning 3.2080-3.2280. Monday's strong HSBC China flash manufacturing PMI gave the ringgit a boost but failed to trigger key chartpoints that could increase momentum for USD/MYR. As such, the dollar is likely to be bounded by the respective entrances to the daily Bollinger downtrend and uptrend channels at 3.2080 and 3.2280. If USD/MYR manages to end the day below 3.2080 and therefore inside the Bollinger downtrend channel, the round-figure trading barrier at 3.2000 will likely break in the near term. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2080 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 3.2000 (round-figure trading barrier), before 3.1870 (base of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.2180 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 3.2280 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2370 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel and daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation. USD/THB remains in consolidation mode within the Ichimoku Cloud support zone that spans 32.36-32.45. The dollar could take on a more supportive tone if it ends the day above the top of the daily Ichimoku Cloud. The situation in Thailand has stabilized since the junta began taking steps to reinvigorate the economy, thus helping the baht to recover to levels seen before the military coup. There is little reason for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate beyond this level for now - barring a broader slide in the U.S. dollar. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.37 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 32.36 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 32.22 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 32.45 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud), then at 32.50 (psychological resistance), before 32.53 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation. USD/PHP continues to hover around the 20-day Bollinger mid, bereft of either technical or fundamental cues to prod it along. The dollar will likely stay trapped in a technical range of 43.70-43.92 - demarcated by the entrance to the daily Bollinger downtrend and uptrend channels respectively - for the near term. Traders may be waiting for a broad move in the U.S. dollar for a trigger in USD/PHP. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.70 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 43.58 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 43.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.80 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 43.92 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 44.00 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. USD/IDR continues to grind higher along the daily Bollinger uptrend channel toward the round-figure trading barrier at 12,000. But a trader said the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could step in to prevent rupiah depreciation past that level - reflecting the market's unwillingness to test the level. If the psychological barrier fails to break for a second time in a week, USD/IDR could instead slip down on capitulation of long-USD positions. The opinion polls for the July 9 Indonesian presidential election appear to show a smaller lead for Joko Widowo, the popular Jakarta governor. If the PDI-P's pro-business candidate fails to win the hot seat, the market could turn negative on rupiah-denominated assets in the near term. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,920 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 11,810 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 11,690 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 12,000 (round-figure trading barrier and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 12,040 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 12,200 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--upside bias. USD/INR has climbed out of the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and is also within the daily Bollinger uptrend channel, and may thus rise toward the weekly Ichimoku Cloud at 60.84 soon. General dollar bullishness may persist as the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury yield rises further past 2.60%, reflecting the market's slightly hawkish view on U.S. interest rates - despite the U.S. Federal Reserve reiterating its dovish stance. Rupee traders are keeping an eye on crude oil prices, wary of spikes that could add to negative pressure on the rupee. India has a significant reliance on oil from Iraq and may face higher fuel bills if oil supply is disrupted due to the escalation in sectarian fighting. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 60.00 (round-figure trading barrier, daily Ichimoku Cloud support, and base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 59.54 (May 22 trendline resistance). Immediate resistance is likely at 60.46 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 60.84 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 61.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 23 Jun 2014 20:46 ET  USD/Asia Mixed, China PMI Effect Fades -- Asia -2-\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 23, 2014 20:46 ET (00:46 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140624ea6o0000p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
