\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Supported, HSBC China PMI Awaited -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,672 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 2014\par 03:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par          Immediate Range   Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.2241-6.2319    6.2113-6.2369 \par USD/TWD   30.000-30.040    29.770-30.140 \par USD/KRW    1,018-1,020      1,015-1,023 \par USD/SGD   1.2489-1.2500    1.2459-1.2519 \par USD/MYR   3.2180-3.2280    3.2080-3.2370 \par USD/THB    32.45-32.50      32.38-32.53 \par USD/PHP    43.69-43.80      43.57-43.91 \par USD/IDR   11,900-12,000    11,790-12,200 \par USD/INR    60.06-60.40      59.93-60.84 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. While the daily USD/CNY parity rate is expected to be stable due to the largely unchanged U.S. dollar index, spot USD/CNY could take on a mildly bullish bias on a Monday close above 6.2369 which would place it above the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and also above the 20-day Bollinger mid line. If this technical barrier is breached, the odds of USD/CNY rising in the near term will increase. \uc2 HSBC\uc2 's preliminary China manufacturing PMI data for June is due at 0145 GMT. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.2241 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.2113 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.2000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 6.2319 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud), then at 3.2369 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 6.2497 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--possible downside bias. The supportive tone in USD/TWD continues as the pair again fails to break the 30.000 round-figure trading barrier on a daily closing basis. The continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been propping up the dollar and deterring bullish bets on the Taiwan dollar. In the offshore nondeliverable forward market, the pricing of the benchmark 1-month contract suggests a neutral to mildly bullish sentiment for the greenback. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.000 (round-figure trading barrier), before 29.770 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.040 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 30.090 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 30.140 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel and daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation. USD/KRW may be rangebound within 1,018-1,021 on an intraday basis, capped by the 20-day Bollinger mid line resistance and supported by the entrance to the daily Bollinger downtrend channel. Recent attempts by the market to push USD/KRW down have been halfhearted, judging by the spikes higher after each attempt to trade lower - a possible sign that the market is wary of \uc2 the Bank of Korea\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  won rises too fast. Unless USD/KRW manages a close below 1,018, the South Korea won may be unable to rally. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,018 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,015 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,010 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 1,020 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1,021 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 1,023 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation. USD/SGD is lingering on the 1.2489 edge of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel as the beacon for USD/Asia - the U.S. dollar index - was little changed overnight. If this technical support is breached by Monday's close, there could be more downside for USD/SGD in the near term. The catalyst for volatility in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  today could be the HSBC China manufacturing PMI due at 0145 GMT. A reading stronger than the 49.7 recorded last month could spur risk appetite for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in general. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2489 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1.2459 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2414 (base of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2500 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1.2508 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 1.2519 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--consolidation. USD/MYR is likely to range between 3.2080-3.2280, bounded by the respective entrances to the daily Bollinger downtrend and uptrend channels. The Malaysia ringgit could get a boost if the HSBC China manufacturing PMI for June comes in better than last month's reading of 49.7. If USD/MYR manages to end the day below 3.2080 and therefore inside the Bollinger downtrend channel, the round-figure trading barrier at 3.2000 will likely break in the near term. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2180 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 3.2080 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 3.2000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 3.2280 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2370 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel and daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--supported. USD/THB is currently in consolidation mode within the Ichimoku Cloud support zone that spans 32.36-32.45. The dollar could take on an even more supportive tone if it ends the day above the daily Ichimoku Cloud. The baht continues to trade on its own merit (or demerit), responding only briefly to the broad U.S. dollar weakness triggered by the less-hawkish-than-expected remarks from the U.S. Federal Reserve last week. Analysts are sceptical of the junta's ability to steer the economy toward a lasting recovery, despite recent announcements of pro-business measures at state-owned firms. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.45 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 32.38 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 32.36 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 32.50 (psychological resistance), then at 32.53 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 32.68 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation. USD/PHP could be trapped in a technical range of 43.69-43.80 demarcated by the entrance to the daily Bollinger downtrend channel and the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance. On a daily close below 43.69, the peso could extend its recent rally. The peso has risen slightly against the U.S. unit since the \uc2 Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its base interest rates unchanged last Thursday while raising the rate on the Special Deposit Account by 0.25 percentage points to reduce liquidity. The counter-inflationary move is likely to find favor with credit rating agencies, and thus will boost investor confidence in the peso. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.69 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 43.57 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 43.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.80 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 43.91 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 44.00 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. USD/IDR retains its bullish technical bias as the daily Bollinger uptrend channel guides the dollar toward a break of the 12,000 round-figure trading barrier. The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might start selling U.S. dollars near that level to prevent a stoploss-related spike in USD/IDR, said one trader. The HSBC China manufacturing PMI reading due at 0145 GMT might be a trigger for volatility in USD/IDR today. Looking slightly further ahead, the July 9 Indonesian presidential election will be the next flashpoint for the rupiah. If the PDI-P's pro-business candidate Joko Widowo fails to win the hot seat, the market could turn negative on rupiah-denominated assets in the near term. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,900 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 11,790 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 11,670 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 12,000 (round-figure trading barrier and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 12,040 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 12,200 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--upside bias. USD/INR has climbed out of the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and is also within the daily Bollinger uptrend channel, and may thus rise toward the weekly Ichimoku Cloud at 60.84 soon. General dollar bullishness could persist as the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury yield holds above 2.60%, reflecting the market's slightly hawkish view on U.S. interest rates - despite the U.S. Federal Reserve reiterating its dovish stance. The spike in oil prices due to further escalation of the Iraq conflict could add to negative pressure on the rupee; India has a substantial reliance on oil from Iraq. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 60.06 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 60.00 (round-figure trading barrier), before 59.93 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 60.40 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 60.84 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 61.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 22, 2014 21:03 ET (01:03 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140623ea6n0000p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
