\par\par \b \uc2 Rise in U.S. 10-Year Yield Supports USD/Asia -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,883 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2014\par 02:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par          Immediate Range   Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.2248-6.2374    6.2122-6.2500 \par USD/TWD   30.000-30.040    29.770-30.140 \par USD/KRW    1,018-1,020      1,015-1,024 \par USD/SGD   1.2492-1.2500    1.2462-1.2524 \par USD/MYR   3.2180-3.2280    3.2080-3.2380 \par USD/THB    32.44-32.50      32.39-32.54 \par USD/PHP    43.79-43.91      43.67-44.00 \par USD/IDR   11,890-12,000    11,770-12,200 \par USD/INR    60.00-60.34      59.85-60.50 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. Spot USD/CNY may be at an inflexion point on the daily chart as it could either drop into the Bollinger downtrend channel at 6.2248 or climb above the Ichimoku Cloud ceiling at 6.2374. Overnight, the U.S. dollar index slipped a little but the rise of the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury yield above 2.60% might worry the U.S. dollar bears. If the Bollinger downtrend channel is activated, the round-figure trading barrier at 6.2000 may break in the near term. The U.S. dollar has been under pressure since the U.S. Federal Reserve chose not to bring forward its timeline for raising interest rates in spite of the recovery of the U.S. economy. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.2248 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.2122 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.2000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 6.2374 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud and 20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 6.2500 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel and round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--possible downside bias. USD/TWD could drop back into the daily Bollinger downtrend channel that begins at 30.050. The slight fall in the U.S. dollar index overnight is likely to weigh on USD/Asia again, though the rise of the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury yield could prompt caution for those short the U.S. dollar. Bullish-USD bets have likely been capitulated after a less-hawkish-than-expected statement from the U.S. Federal Reserve. But USD/TWD downside may not be forthcoming until the round-figure trading barrier at 30.000 is breached on a daily closing basis. There is a strong likelihood that the \uc2 Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been propping up the greenback to prevent excessive Taiwan dollar strength. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.000 (round-figure trading barrier), before 29.770 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.040 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 30.090 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 30.140 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel and daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation. USD/KRW has rebounded off the week's low triggered by the U.S. FOMC meeting and may now consolidate within a range of 1,018-1,021. USD/KRW has shown resilience in spite of bearishness for the greenback after the U.S. Federal Reserve disappointed the market by not adopting a more hawkish stance on Wednesday. The inability to confirm entry into the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at 1,018 is a sign that buying on dips in USD/KRW is prevalent. The fear of \uc2 the Bank of Korea\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  won rises too much could be keeping USD/KRW afloat. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,018 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,015 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,010 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 1,020 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1,021 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 1,024 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation. USD/SGD has rebounded back out of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel and may now be caught in a rut between the entrance to the downtrend channel at 1.2492 and the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone at 1.2508. A clear break of these technical barriers is needed for a stronger clue as to USD/SGD's next move. While the U.S. Federal Reserve chose not to turn more hawkish at its FOMC meeting Wednesday, the market seems unconvinced that interest rates will stay low very much longer. The overnight rise of the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury yield may be a sign that traders expect the Fed will have to raise interest rates sooner - as the U.S. economy consistently improves. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2492 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1.2462 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2419 (base of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2500 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1.2508 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 1.2524 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--consolidation. USD/MYR is likely to range between 3.2080-3.2280, bounded by the respective entrances to the daily Bollinger downtrend and uptrend channels. The overnight rise of the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury yield back above 2.60% reflects the market's underlying bullishness for U.S. interest rates -- and thereby the dollar -- despite the U.S. Federal Reserve's dovish stance at its Wednesday FOMC meeting. If the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yield curve remains buoyant, the greenback is unlikely to fall much. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2180 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 3.2080 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 3.2000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 3.2280 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2380 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2440 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--supported. USD/THB is back above the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone and could hence stay elevated above 32.44. The baht continues to trade on its own merit (or demerit), responding only briefly to the broad U.S. dollar weakness triggered by the less-hawkish-than-expected remarks from the U.S. Federal Reserve on Wednesday. If USD/THB rallies off the Cloud support and rises above the 20-day Bollinger mid line at 32.54, more upside might be available for the greenback. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.44 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 32.39 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 32.36 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 32.50 (psychological resistance), then at 32.54 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 32.69 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation. USD/PHP could be trapped in a technical range of 43.79-43.91 for now as bearishness for the U.S. dollar -- triggered by a dovish U.S. Federal Reserve -- has faded. The greenback could find support at the 20-day Bollinger mid line at 43.79 and could even take on a bullish technical bias if it ends Friday above 43.91 - the entrance to the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. The \uc2 Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its base interest rates unchanged on Thursday, as expected by analysts polled by the Wall Street Journal, while raising the rate on the Special Deposit Account by 0.25 percentage point to reduce liquidity and combat inflationary pressures. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.79 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 43.67 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.91 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 44.00 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 44.03 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 44.18 (200-day moving average and Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. USD/IDR continues to climb higher along its daily Bollinger uptrend channel, almost oblivious to the broad U.S. dollar rally seen on Thursday. While the dovish tone of the U.S. FOMC meeting gave USD/IDR a setback -- sending it to the base of the uptrend channel briefly -- the bullish technical signal was kept intact by Thursday's close above 11,890. A new four-month peak could be notched if USD/IDR surpasses Wednesday's 12,000 watermark. An offshore trader said there is a strong likelihood that the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may try to slow the rupiah's fall if it shoots past the round-figure trading barrier of 12,000 - which could activate stoploss orders in the market that will cause a spike for the dollar. Looking slightly further ahead, the July 9 Indonesian presidential election will be the next flashpoint for the rupiah. If the PDI-P's pro-business candidate Joko Widowo fails to win the hot seat, the market could turn negative on rupiah-denominated assets in the near term. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,890 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 11,770 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 11,650 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 12,000 (round-figure trading barrier and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 12,030 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 12,200 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 19 Jun 2014 20:59 ET  Rise in U.S. 10-Year Yield Supports USD/Asia -- -2-\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation. USD/INR may still be stuck inside the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone spanning 59.85-60.06 after it failed to break lower Thursday on the bearish-USD tone triggered by the U.S. Federal Reserve's dovish stance on interest rates. There could be upside potential for USD/INR if it ends Friday above 60.06 - which would place it within the daily bollinger uptrend channel and above the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone. The overnight rise of the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury yield back above 2.60% reflects the market's underlying bullishness for U.S. interest rates - and thereby the dollar. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 60.00 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 59.85 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel and base of daily Ichimoku Cloud), before 59.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 60.06 (top of Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 60.34 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 60.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 19, 2014 20:59 ET (00:59 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140620ea6k00010\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
