\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea May  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves rise by most in 7 months after suspected  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 249 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2014\par 23:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, June 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves rose to a record high $360.91 billion in May, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Thursday, rising $5.07 billion from the previous month in the biggest increase in seven months.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea\uc2 , in a statement, credited the increase last month to gains from management of the reserves. May is the 11th straight month they hit a record.\par \par \uc2 The increase also came after \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders suspected authorities took part in dollar-buying market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times last month to slow the won's strengthening against the dollar.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to curb volatility and in May, aimed to contain the won's swift appreciation which is seen as damaging to the country's exporters.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently up more than 3 percent against the dollar this year.\par \par \uc2 May's increase in reserves was the largest since a rise of $6.30 billion in October 2013.\par \par \uc2 South Korea's reserves are the seventh biggest in the world and during May, 91.5 percent were in the form of securities.\par \par \uc2 South Korean foreign reserves (in $ bln, at end-month, rounded): May Apr Mar Feb Jan Dec Nov 360.91 355.85 354.34 351.79 348.39 346.46 345.01 (Reporting by Christine Kim; E