\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korean won steady on suspected  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , stocks inch down\b0\par\par\uc2 495 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2014\par 04:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Won weakens despite record current account surplus data\par     * Stocks steady, underpinned by persistent foreign inflows\par \par     SEOUL, May 29 (Reuters) - The South Korean won held its ground on\par Thursday morning, even as local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were spotted\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to limit gains from exporters' month-end dollar flows and a\par record-high current account surplus in April.\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was quoted at 1,021.7 against the dollar as of\par 0210 GMT, compared with Wednesday's onshore close at 1,021.4.\par     "Suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted at start of the session, although the\par scale of dollar-purchases didn't seem that strong," a foreign bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par dealer said.\par     The won eased to an intraday low of 1,022.9 in the opening minutes, but\par gradually gained on demand by exporters.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were spotted  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through\par dollar purchases earlier this month, taming the pace of the won's appreciation\par and successfully supporting the 1,020 USD/KRW level. \par     South Korea's current account surplus in April surged to a record to $9.81\par billion on a seasonally adjusted basis from March's revised $6.6 billion surplus\par as exports rose sharply, adding upward pressure to the already-bouyant\par won. \par     "The 1,020 level for USD/KRW pair should hold up. The greenback is gaining\par traction against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  now, and is widely expected to\par strengthen further, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai\f28 \uc2 \f2  Futures' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst Lee Dae-ho.\par     He added the won's upward pressures will gradually diminish should the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ease policy to shore up growth, while South Korean \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities offset exporters' month-end \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flows.\par     The won has strengthened 4.2 percent against the dollar this quarter,\par outperforming its regional peers.\par     Meanwhile, the Korea Composite Stock Price Index (KOSPI) was down\par 0.1 percent at 2,014.70 points as of 0210 GMT. \par     The main bourse rose 1 percent in the previous session, triggering some\par profit-taking by retail and local institutional investors who combined to sell a\par net 53.7 billion won ($52.58 million).\par     Foreign investors positioned as net buyers in the morning by scooping up\par 56.3 billion won worth of KOSPI shares, headed for a 13th straight session of\par net purchasing. \par     Foreigners have driven the market 2.6 percent higher in the latest buying\par spree, bringing in 2.6 trillion won.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the world's biggest handset maker and one of the\par beneficiaries from the foreign influx, rose 1.9 percent to underpin the broader\par index.\par     \par                       0210 GMT    Prev close\par  Dollar/won            1,021.7       1,021.4\par  Yen/won           10.0521/462       10.0295\par  *K