\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea stocks hold steady near 5-1/2-month peak, won flat\b0\par\par\uc2 388 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2014\par 05:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Offshore investors headed for 9th day of net buying\par     * Won flat amid \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  caution\par \par     SEOUL, May 23 (Reuters) - Seoul shares were nearly flat on\par Friday, staying close to a 5-1/2-month high hit the previous day\par as foreign inflows offset profit-taking by retail and domestic\par institutional investors, while the won was also little\par changed.\par     The Korea Composite Stock Price Index (KOSPI) was \par down 0.1 percent at 2,014.08 points as of 0300 GMT. On the week,\par the index is up 0.1 percent.\par     "The solid factory surveys from the major economies went by\par well, and the market is digesting the previous session's relief\par rally," said Bae Sung-young, an analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The U.S. manufacturing sector expanded at a\par stronger-than-expected rate in May, while factory output growth\par hit its fastest pace since February 2011, an industry report\par showed on Thursday. \par     "Now all eyes are on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's meeting in\par June. Until then, the market moves will solely depend on foreign\par inflows," he added.\par     Foreign investors bought a net 54.8 billion won ($53.5\par million) of KOSPI shares by midday, poised for a ninth straight\par session of net buying, while retail and local institutional\par investors sold a combined 57 billion won worth.\par     Overseas investors bought 2.3 trillion won worth of stocks\par over an eight-day net buying streak through Thursday.\par     Steelmaker POSCO fell 1.1 percent, as investors\par locked in gains from Thursday, while market heavyweight \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung\par Electronics Co Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  shed 0.5 percent.\par     The won was nearly unchanged in subdued trade, with\par caution over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities offsetting demand from exporters.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was quoted at 1,024.1 against the\par dollar as of 0300 GMT, compared with Thursday's onshore close at\par 1,024.2. On a weekly basis, the won was flat.\par                        0300 GMT    Prev close\par  Dollar/won            1,024.1       1,024.2\par  Yen/won           10.0678/599       10.0639\par  *KTB futures           106.00        105.96\par  KOSPI                2,014.08      2,015.59\par  * Front-month futures on three-year treasury bonds\par ($1 = 1024.2500 Korean Won)\par \par  (Reporting by Jungmin Jang; Editing by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chris Gallagher\f28 \uc2 \f2 )\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-5-26T03:32:45.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140523ea5n003v0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
