\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupee rises more on hopes of clear opposition victory; won gains\b0\par\par\uc2 477 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Mai 2014\par 10:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Updates prices. For midday report, double-click\par  )\par     SINGAPORE, May 13 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee extended\par gains on Tuesday as exit polls suggested pro-reform and\par business-friendly opposition parties had won elections, while\par the South Korean won rose on exporters' demand for settlements.\par     The rupee advanced as much as 0.8 percent to 59.59\par per dollar as Indian stocks hit a record high for a\par third consecutive session.\par     The partially convertible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  later pared some of its\par gains as traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb its strength. \par     Hindu nationalist Narendra Modi is set to become India's\par next prime minister, four major exit polls showed on Monday,\par with his opposition party the Bharatiya Janata Party and its\par allies forecast to sweep to a parliamentary majority in the\par world's biggest-ever election. \par     The won gained on bids from exporters such as\par shipbuilders and as foreigners' demand lifted Seoul shares\par .\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were suspected of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the won's gains, even though their dollar\par bids became weaker in the afternoon, traders said.\par     Meanwhile, the Philippine peso fell as interbank\par speculators continued to take profits from the best performing\par emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the last week.\par     The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor earlier said it was\par ready to guard against excesses in the financial system such as\par a possible increase in investment flows after last week's credit\par rating upgrade from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0800 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       102.33         102.11       -0.21\par  *Sing dlr        1.2515         1.2507       -0.06\par   Taiwan dlr      30.202         30.192       -0.03\par   Korean won     1021.75        1024.40       +0.26\par  *Baht             32.60          32.61       +0.03\par   Peso             43.82          43.71       -0.24\par   Rupiah        11530.00       11516.00       -0.12\par   Rupee            59.85          60.05       +0.33\par  *Ringgit         3.2370         3.2385       +0.05\par   Yuan            6.2309         6.2365       +0.09\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       102.33         105.28       +2.88\par   Sing dlr        1.2515         1.2632       +0.93\par   Taiwan dlr      30.202         29.950       -0.83\par   Korean won     1021.75        1055.40       +3.29\par   Baht             32.60          32.86       +0.80\par   Peso             43.82          44.40       +1.32\par   Rupiah        11530.00       12160.00       +5.46\par   Rupee            59.85          61.80       +3.26\par   Ringgit         3.2370         3.2755       +1.19\par   Yuan            6.2309         6.0539       -2.84\par   * Financial markets in Malaysia,