\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Sentiment more bullish on Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , yuan sentiment best in 2 months but still bearish\b0\par\par\uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2014\par 10:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Short yuan positions smallest since late February\par     * Bullish Singapore dollar bets largest since Sept 2012\par     * Long won, Taiwan dollar positions highest since Jan 2013\par \par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, May 8 (Reuters) - Sentiment toward emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  improved in the last two weeks as the Chinese yuan\par stabilised and as the U.S. Federal Reserve is expected to keep\par interest rates low for some time, a Reuters poll showed on\par Thursday.\par     Bearish bets on the yuan fell to the lowest since\par late February, when sentiment on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  started to sour,\par according to the survey of 13 analysts conducted on Wednesday\par and Thursday.\par     The renminbi has gained strongly this week, showing signs of\par reversing a four-month slide. \par     Traders questioned whether the recent gains were a signal\par that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had switched its stance to gently\par supporting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after aggressively driving it lower this\par year to deter speculators from thinking it was a one-way\par appreciation bet.\par     The poll also showed long positions in the Singapore dollar\par  hit the highest level since September 2012. The\par city-state's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is often used as a proxy to bet the yuan's\par moves.\par     Bullish bets on the South Korean won and the\par Taiwan dollar reached their highest levels since\par January 2013.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit a near six-year high this week\par as foreign investors snapped up the country's financial assets,\par especially bonds, and on demand from exporters for settlements.\par     Caution increased over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South\par Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to stem the won's\par appreciation. However, the authorities have not been\par aggressively \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , local traders said.\par     The Taiwan dollar also gained on inflows of foreign\par financial institutions.\par     Sentiment on the ringgit was the most optimistic\par since May last year as the Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose on the yuan's\par rebound.\par     Long positions in the Philippine peso touched a\par six-month high on stock inflows and as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is\par expected to raise reserve requirements later on Thursday.\par     Bullish bets on the Indian rupee also increased on\par equity inflows, while investors stayed cautious ahead of the\par conclusion of general elections next week.\par     In the previous survey, sentiment on emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had deteriorated on sustained weakness in the yuan.\par  \par     Meanwhile, short positions in the Thai baht rose\par slightly on increasing political unrest.\par     On Wednesday, a Thai court ordered Prime Minister Yingluck\par Shinawatra to step down after finding her guilty of abuse of\par power, prolonging a political crisis that has led to violent\par protests and brought the economy close to recession.\par  \par     The Reuters survey is focused on what analysts believe are\par the current market positions in nine Asian emerging market\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : the Chinese yuan, South Korean won, Singapore\par dollar, Indonesian rupiah, Taiwan dollar, Indian rupee,\par Philippine peso PHP=PDSP, Malaysian ringgit and the Thai baht.\par     The poll uses estimates of net long or short positions on a\par scale of minus 3 to plus 3.\par     A score of plus 3 indicates the market is significantly long\par U.S. dollars. The figures included positions held through\par non-deliverable forwards (NDFs).\par     The survey findings ASIAPOSN are provided below (positions\par in U.S. dollar versus each \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ):\par  DATE     CNY   KRW   SGD   IDR   TWD   INR   MYR   PHP   THB\par  8-May    0.31 -1.50 -0.74 -0.40 -0.60 -0.90 -0.65 -0.46  0.17\par  24-Apr   0.73 -0.88  0.08 -0.33 -0.02 -0.32 -0.17  0.07  0.13\par  10-Apr   0.69 -1.12 -0.68 -1.00 -0.34 -1.14 -0.64  0.07  0.10\par  27-Mar   0.80  0.27  0.07 -0.72  0.55 -1.06 -0.22  0.13  0.35\par  13-Mar   0.41 -0.01  0.23 -1.28  0.35 -1.22 -0.43 -0.18  0.07\par  27-Feb   0.00 -0.09 -0.07 -0.87  0.52 -0.40 -0.31  0.14  0.59\par  13-Feb  -0.90 -0.66 -0.38  0.02  0.48 -0.20  0.28  0.16  0.35\par  30-Jan  -1.15 -0.01  0.14  0.85  0.46  0.22  0.48  0.53  0.93\par  16-Jan  -1.58 -0.57  0.51  0.88  0.36 -0.46  0.53  0.66  0.90\par  3-Jan   -1.73 -1.09  0.47  1.34 -0.03 -0.37  0.53  0.48  1.38\par  \par  (Additional reporting by Shaloo Shrivastava in BANGALORE;\par Editing by Kim Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-5-8T09:01:29.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140508ea5800ci5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
