\par\par \b \uc2 South Korea's Won Touches Six-Year High Against The Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kwanwoo Jun \par \uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 April 2014\par 14:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 South Korea's won touched a six-year high against the dollar Tuesday, as the country reported a strong export performance in March.\par \par \uc2 Asia's fourth-largest economy has in the past been chided by the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  for keeping its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  intentionally low to make its exports cheaper. The fund earlier this month said the won could be up to 8% undervalued.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth fluctuations. Either way, analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  this time appears to be allowing the won to appreciate.\par \par \uc2 "Financial authorities were much less aggressive in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets than before," Samsung Futures \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst Jeon Seung-ji said. "The authorities seem to act to the growing pressure for the won to appreciate in line with the country's strong economic fundamentals, backed by the widening current account surplus."\par \par \uc2 South Korea's current account surplus rose to a five-month high of $7.35 billion in March, up from the previous month's revised $4.5 billion, said \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2 . The brisk exports of mobile handsets, vehicles and semiconductor chips on growing demand from the U.S., Europe and Southeast Asian markets helped push the current surplus to the highest since October 2013, the BOK said. The current account has been in the black since March 2012.\par \par \uc2 On a seasonally-adjusted basis, the surplus narrowed to $6.65 billion in March from a revised $7.54 billion in February due to growing imports.\par \par \uc2 "Continued current account surpluses, exposure to improving U.S. and euro area economic activity, which together take roughly 20% of Korea's total exports, and a likely increase in domestic demand bode well for a further pickup in portfolio inflows and won appreciation," said \uc2 Barclays\uc2  economist Wai Ho Leong.\par \par \uc2 "In addition, recent (won) appreciation and relatively modest Bank of Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggests that the Korean authorities are more comfortable with a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 ING economist Tim Condon said the won "is no longer an attractive vehicle for speculation" because of \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2 's reduced \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which means more two-way risk in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The won was relatively weak against a number of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  between the financial crisis and 2012, allowing South Korea to increase its share of global trade.\par \par \uc2 After underperforming other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first quarter, the won has appreciated more than 4% against the U.S. greenback over the past month.\par \par \uc2 The won's strength against Japan's yen has led to public complaints in recent months from South Korean officials.\par \par \uc2 Me. Leong of \uc2 Barclays\uc2  expects the won to strengthen to 1,020.00 against the U.S. dollar in the next year versus 1,030.60 in late onshore trade in Seoul on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 ING economist Mr. Condon said he expects the won to strengthen to 1,015 against the U.S. dollar by the end of this year.\par \par \uc2 Write to Kwanwoo Jun at kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 29, 2014 08:46 ET (12:46 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140429ea4t0024q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
