\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won at 6-year high on current account, Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  edges up before Fed\b0\par\par\uc2 880 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 April 2014\par 06:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * S.Korea sees 34th straight month of C/A surplus\par     * Some suspects S.Korea \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     * Taiwan dollar rises on stock inflows; importers limit\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, April 29 (Reuters) - The South Korean won hit a\par fresh six-year high on Tuesday, leading gains among emerging\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , though many investors remained cautious ahead\par of major events this week including a U.S. Federal Reserve\par policy meeting.\par     The won advanced after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data showed\par South Korea posted its 34th consecutive monthly current account\par surplus in March thanks to resilient exports and low prices of\par imported raw materials. \par     The Taiwan dollar rose on stock inflows.\par     "China's economy is not as bad as initially feared, so the\par won and the Taiwan dollar would be the best beneficiaries," said\par Yuna Park, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bond analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dongbu Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  in\par Seoul.\par     "A soft yuan may be an obstacle, but improving developed\par economies will help them weather it," Park added.\par     China's economy grew 7.4 percent in the first quarter from a\par year earlier, its slowest pace in 18 months, but that was\par slightly higher than market expectations. April factory activity\par in the world's second largest economy shrank but the pace of\par decline eased.  \par     Economic growth in South Korea during the first quarter was\par higher than expectations, while Taiwan's economy in the period\par is seen growing faster than the previous quarter.\par   \par     Their hi-tech exports have proven more resilient to the\par global slowdown than Southeast Asian countries which are heavily\par dependent on exports of commodities and raw materials.\par     Still, traders remained wary of potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Taiwan to stem\par their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ' gains.\par     Investors were also awaiting the Fed's two-day policy\par meeting, which starts later in the day, and April U.S. jobs data\par  on Friday.\par     \par     WON\par     The won rose as much as 0.4 percent to 1,030.6 per dollar,\par its strongest since August 2008, on sustained month-end demand\par from local exporters.\par     South Korea reported a current account surplus of $6.65\par billion in March on a seasonally adjusted basis, down from a\par revised $7.54 billion surplus in February, but still\par substantial.\par     "Another large Korean current account surplus in March\par reaffirms Korea's strong economic fundamentals and supports the\par recent KRW appreciation, in our view," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a client\par note, referring to the won.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  revised up its one-month forecast for the won's\par value to 1,040 from 1,070, its three-month forecast to 1,030\par from 1,060 as well as its six- and 12-month forecasts to 1,020\par from 1,050, respectively.\par     The bank also revised up 2014 current account balance\par forecast for the second time this year to $73 billion from $65.5\par billion, compared to $79.9 billion surplus last year.\par     Some traders suspected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities of\par buying dollar to stem strength in the won with caution\par increasing over their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Finance ministry and the new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief warned\par against a sharp gains in the South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on April 10\par when it rose to as firm as 1,031.4.\par     A couple of closes firmer than 1,032 is seen helping the won\par head to a psychologically important 1,000, analysts said.\par     \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par     The Taiwan dollar gained as inflows from foreign financial\par inflows lifted local shares.\par     Exporters were not active, while importers took slides in\par the U.S. dollar as chances to buy it for payments, limiting the\par island's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains, traders said.\par     Last week, exporters bought much of the Taiwan dollar for\par settlements, so their month-end demand was not seen strong,\par traders added.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has not been spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while\par investors remained wary of its purchases of the U.S. dollar,\par according to traders.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0420 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       102.48         102.48       +0.00\par   Sing dlr        1.2565         1.2566       +0.01\par   Taiwan dlr      30.181         30.285       +0.34\par   Korean won     1031.50        1035.00       +0.34\par   Baht             32.26 