\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1 -South Korean won hits near 6-yr high, set for more gains\b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2014\par 03:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, April 9 (Reuters) - The South Korean won looked set to build on its strength after climbing to a near six-year high early on Wednesday, spurred by a broadly weaker dollar and foreign buying of Seoul stocks, particularly in the likes of global heavyweight \uc2 Samsung Electronics\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was hobbled by fading expectations of additional near-term stimulus in Japan and Europe, which buoyed the yen and the euro.\par \par \uc2 The South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also attracted support on optimism over corporate earnings and a steadily recovering trend in Asia's fourth-largest economy.\par \par \uc2 The won rose as high as 1,043.4 against the dollar in morning trade, the strongest mark since Aug. 18 2008. It was last quoted at 1,044.4 as of 0128 GMT, up 0.8 percent from Tuesday's domestic close at 1,052.2.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar has been on the downside due to the lack of fresh policy easing in Japan and Europe and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are also getting a boost," said Lee Dae-ho, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Hyundai Futures Co.\par \par \uc2 "The (\b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) authorities are unlikely to carry out strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as long as the current market movements are in line with the global patterns," he said, adding the won's short-term trend would likely remain upward.\par \par \uc2 Investors who had gone long on the dollar were forced to unwind their positions, partly as the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  gave no indication it was preparing to offer fresh stimulus in the short term.\par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have also suggested no urgency for any immediate policy action.\par \par \uc2 In Seoul's main stock exchange, the benchmark KOSPI briefly rose above a psychological barrier of 2,000 points on Wednesday as foreigners extended their buying streak. The index was last quoted up 0.15 percent at 1,996.03 points at 0128 GMT. (Reporting by Jungmin Jang; Editing by Choonsik Yoo & Shri Navaratnam)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-4-12T01:33:39.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140409ea49002gy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
