\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  bounces on Turkey's bold defence of lira, won shines\b0\par\par\uc2 990 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2014\par 06:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Offshore funds cover won short positions\par     * Ringgit gains on hedge funds, demand vs Sing dlr\par     * Real money sell ringgit on rallies -traders\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 29 (Reuters) - The South Korean won led a\par relief rally among emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday as a\par huge interest rate hike by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  calmed emerging\par markets after several days of turmoil. \par     Turkey followed India by tightening policy at a midnight\par meeting of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with the massive hike in the\par overnight lending rate of 425 basis points taking rates all the\par way to 12 percent.  \par     "Aggressive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Turkish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  move produces a global\par 'good', sucking the life out of the USD against EM Asia,"\par Scotiabank said in a research note.\par     The won also benefited from\par stronger-than-expected industrial output growth and a record\par current account surplus. The won's strength lifted the Taiwan\par dollar.\par     Malaysia's ringgit advanced on buying by offshore\par hedge funds and demand against the Singapore dollar.\par     Asian shares also rallied after Turkey's move, reflecting a\par broad rise in risk-appetite which provided some respite for the\par battered Turkish lira.\par     Scoatiabank said that most Asian central banks are unlikely\par to tighten monetary policy, given better economic fundamentals\par in the region and expectations of a further reduction in the\par U.S. Federal Reserve's stimulus.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to keep its interest\par rate unchanged at 3.00 percent later in the day.\par     Still, emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  face a bumpy road, analysts\par say.\par     "While the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Turkish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's 'no-holds-barred' rate\par hikes may provide a near term respite for emerging market\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the near term, background caution nonetheless will\par continue to persist," \f28 \uc2 \f2 OCBC Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a client note.\par     "We continue to see key risks to Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the\par depletion of portfolio capital flow interest, dollar dynamics,\par as well as a potential flare up in EM jitters."\par     The recent selloff in emerging market assets drove Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sharply lower as investors fretted over the twin\par concerns of a cutback in U.S. stimulus and slowing growth in\par China.\par     The Fed is expected to announce another $10 billion cut in\par its monthly bond-purchase programme when it concludes a two-day\par policy meeting later in the day.\par     \par     WON\par     The won rose as offshore funds scrambled to cover short\par positions and on demand from exporters such as shipbuilders,\par traders said.\par     South Korea's industrial output jumped in December and its\par current account surplus grew to a record last year, suggesting\par the economy carried strong momentum into 2014 with sufficient\par buffers to weather the latest global market turmoil.\par  \par     Some traders added dollar holdings ahead of the result of\par the Fed's policy meeting later in the day, limiting the won's\par upside.\par     "As the Fed is expected to continue to taper, the won will\par find some resistance at 1,070," said a foreign bank trader in\par Singapore, referring to the won's value against the dollar.\par     Domestic importers also purchased the greenback for\par payments, while some traders suspected that authorities were\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep the won below 1,070.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's financial markets will be closed on Thursday\par and Friday to mark the Lunar New Year holidays.\par     \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par     The Taiwan dollar gained as local interbank speculators\par bought it on the won's strength.\par     Trading was subdued with little corporate flows as the\par island's financial markets will be shut from Thursday to Tuesday\par for the Lunar New Year holidays.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit advanced on the U.S. dollar on demand from\par leverage funds after Turkey's rate hikes improved risk\par sentiment.\par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also rose 0.2 percent to 2.6080\par against the Singapore dollar. On Tuesday, the ringgit\par hit 2.6225 to the neighboring unit, its weakest since July 1998.\par     "We see scope for ringgit to benefit more from the near-term\par improvement in EM sentiment following the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par Turkey\f28 \uc2 \f2 's decision to aggressively hike interest rates," ANZ said\par in a research note.\par     ANZ recommends buying the ringgit to the Singapore dollar\par through one-month forward/non-deliverable forward for a\par short-term tactical trade.\par     Against the U.S. dollar, however, some real money funds and\par local traders sold the ringgit around its session high of\par 3.3160, traders said.\par     "The question is whether the risk rally can continue," said\par a senior Malaysian bank trader in Kuala Lumpur.\par     "I will pick levels possibly next week to short risk\par positions after the Fed. Turkey just saved themselves for the\par short term with fundamental problems still there," the trader\par said.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0430 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       103.23         102.93       -0.29\par   Sing dlr        1.2724         1.2746       +0.17\par   Taiwan dlr      30.288         30.451       +0.54\par   Korean won     1070.40        1081.20       +1.01\par   Baht             32.87          32.91       +0.12\par   Peso             45.14          45.23       +0.21\par   Rupiah        12140.00       12185.00       +0.37\par   Rupee            62.17          62.51       +0.55\par   Ringgit         3.3200         3.3350       +0.45\par   Yuan            6.0548         6.0508       -0.07\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       103.23         105.28       +1.98\par   Sing dlr        1.2724         1.2632       -0.72\par   Taiwan dlr      30.288         29.950       -1.12\par   Korean won     1070.40        1055.40       -1.40\par   Baht             32.87          32.86       -0.03\par   Peso             45.14          44.40       -1.64\par   Rupiah        12140.00       12160.00       +0.16\par   Rupee            62.17          61.80       -0.60\par   Ringgit         3.3200         3.2755       -1.34\par   Yuan            6.0548         6.0539       -0.01\par     \par \par  (Additional reporting by Roger Tung in TAIPEI; Editing by Shri\par Navaratnam)\par \f28 