\par\par \b \uc2 IMF Questions South Korea's  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Policy\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ian Talley   \par \uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2014\par 01:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON--The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  on Wednesday questioned \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, telling Seoul that it should only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in exchange-rate markets to prevent volatility that might damage the economy.\par \par \uc2 The unusually explicit scrutiny of Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy comes after Bank of Korea's top official indicated early this year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to curb the won's strength. It also follows U.S. criticism late last year in which the Treasury Department said it was concerned that Korea had resumed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and needed to be more transparent about its activities.\par \par \uc2 "The won should continue to be market determined, with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited to smoothing disorderly market conditions," the IMF's executive board said in a statement on the annual review of the country's economy.\par \par \uc2 The fund says the won is "moderately undervalued," accounting for inflation, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is coming under increased appreciation pressure by markets as the emerging market outperforms many of its peers.\par \par \uc2 Korean officials say their efforts are meant to stabilize markets. But some U.S. economists say Korea wants to keep a lid on the value of the exchange rate to bar exports from becoming too expensive.\par \par \uc2 Although countries can devalue their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it comes at the expense of other countries' exchange rates rising and can fuel trade and political tensions between governments.\par \par \uc2 To avoid creating friction over \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies, the IMF said, Korea should be more candid about its exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 IMF directors "considered that increased transparency in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would help enhance the credibility of the authorities' exchange rate policy," the fund said.\par \par \uc2 The executive board appeared to be divided, however, about whether the country should continue to build up foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buffers to protect against potential economic crises.\par \par \uc2 "Some directors considered that the current level of reserves is adequate and does not warrant further accumulation, while a few others, noting the proven benefits of building a strong buffer in past crises, cautioned against prejudging the case," the board said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ian Talley at ian.talley@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 23-01-14 0040GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020140123ea1n0000c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
