\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 513 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2014\par 02:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TREASURY SECRETARY LEW: U.S. TO EXHAUST DEBT LIMIT EMERGENCY POWERS IN LATE FEBRUARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury Secretary Jacob Lew on Wednesday said the government would exhaust its borrowing powers by late February if Congress doesn't act to raise or suspend the debt ceiling before that time, which matches the more conservative estimate previously disclosed. (published 2123 GMT Wednesday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK OF CANADA GOV. POLOZ SAYS 'DOOR SLIGHTLY MORE OPEN' TO RATE CUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stephen Poloz\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Canada's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor, said that the door to a rate cut is "slightly more open," after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2  issued an interest-rate statement that ramped up concern over persistently below-target inflation earlier Wednesday. (published 0004 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SOUTH KOREA 4TH-QUARTER GDP GROWTH SLOWS, MEETS VIEW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's economic growth slowed as expected in the final quarter of last year on weaker construction spending, despite robust exports that reaffirms a recovery in Asia's fourth-largest economy. (published 2324 GMT Wednesday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IMF QUESTIONS SOUTH KOREA'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  POLICY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Wednesday questioned \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy, telling Seoul that it should only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in exchange-rate markets to prevent volatility that might damage the economy. (published 2317 GMT Wednesday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK 2013 CAR PRODUCTION HITS HIGHEST LEVEL SINCE 2007 - SMMT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. car production rose 3.1% last year to its highest level since 2007, driven by home demand and exports outside Europe, putting the resurgent British industry on course to overtake France as the continent's third-biggest car-making country. (published 0001 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NZ MANUFACTURING ACTIVITY EXPANDS FOR 15TH MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's manufacturing activity expanded for a fifteenth consecutive month in December, although activity slowed slightly from the previous month, data released Thursday showed. (published 2201 GMT Wednesday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par VIETNAM'S SURGE ENCOURAGES IPOS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors are warming to Vietnamese stocks, wagering on accelerating growth in an often overlooked economy. (published 2356 GMT Wednesday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par U.S. SEES ASIA-PACIFIC TRADE TALKS RESUMING NEXT MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 High-level negotiations to form an Asia-Pacific trade agreement likely will resume next month, a top U.S. trade official said Wednesday. (published 2106 GMT Wednesday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI EMERGENCY LAW FAILS TO QUELL CRISIS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The first day of a state of emergency began here Wednesday with raucous street protests and more questions about whether Thailand's army would step in to take control as civil unrest continues to trouble the country. (published 0033 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TURKEY SELLS $2.5 BILLION, 10-YEAR BOND AT 5.85% YIELD -- SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turkey issued its first dollar bond this year, selling $2.5 billion in debt to unexpectedly strong demand even as the sovereign paid a higher premium than prior years. (published 2306 GMT Wednesday) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par DRAWING A BEAD ON INDIA'S INFLATION TARGET -- HEARD ON THE STREET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Raghuram Rajan's project of fixing India's dilapidated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  now has a plan. Sticking to it could prove tumultuous for investors. (published 0049 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 22, 2014 20:00 ET (01:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140123ea1n00048\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
