\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Bullish as U.S. Stocks Slip -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,929 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2014\par 01:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0500-6.0550   6.0400-6.0600 \par USD/TWD   30.000-30.105   29.910-30.200 \par USD/KRW    1,062-1,065     1,060-1,070 \par USD/SGD   1.2633-1.2688   1.2600-1.2700 \par USD/MYR   3.2800-3.2950   3.2710-3.3000 \par USD/THB    33.00-33.13     32.80-33.20 \par USD/PHP    44.50-44.74     44.26-44.80 \par USD/IDR   12,150-12,278   12,000-12,300 \par USD/INR    62.14-62.41     62.00-62.70 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. The PBOC's daily USD/CNY benchmark rate could be set slightly lower Tuesday to reflect the overnight slippage in the U.S. dollar index, which would guide spot USD/CNY back down toward the record low of 6.0500 touched last week. Investor appetite for Chinese assets may however be tempered by recently lacklustre economic data, including Monday's services PMI figure which was below expectations. China stocks may still be under pressure as the Shanghai Composite Index sinks lower, guided by the daily Bollinger downtrend channel, toward the psychological support at 2,000. Looking slightly further ahead, traders await China trade data due Wednesday. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.0500 (record low and psychological support), before 6.0400 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.0550 (lower Bollinger band standard deviation 2), then at 6.0600 (psychological resistance), before 6.0687 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--upside bias. The Taiwan dollar looks set to weaken further as the dollar surges above the psychological barrier of 30.000. However, the overnight slippage of the U.S. dollar index could help cap USD/TWD. Suspected dollar-buying by the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  created a spike to 30.301 on Monday. Traders holding short dollar positions are likely to use any dips to cover their positions as broad greenback strength continues. Traders will be watching the NDF market for signs that the short-covering is done; the price difference between the 1-month USD/TWD non-deliverable forward contract and the spot price remains positive--a sign of strong dollar demand. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.000 (psychological support), then at 29.910 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 29.800 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.105 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.200 (psychological resistance), before 30.301 (Monday's 6-month high).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation. USD/KRW remains at elevated levels after the spike on Monday which was triggered by widespread USD short-covering on fear that the \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to quell won strength. USD/KRW is now at the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel and may thus consolidate for now, supported by the Ichimoku Cloud base at 1,062. The threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2 --due to comments late last week from BOK officials that they are closely monitoring the won's volatility--likely triggered the won selloff. The BOK comments came on the back of the won touching a new 5-year high against the Japanese yen last week. The \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  occasionally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market to ensure exchange rate-related price competitiveness for local exporters versus Japanese rivals. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,062 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud), then at 1,060 (psychological support and base of Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,056 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 1,065 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,070 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation. USD/SGD appears to be lacking momentum to trade much higher, judging by several failed attempts to enter the Bollinger uptrend channel which now caps at 1.2688. Until the Bollinger uptrend channel comes into play, USD/SGD is likely to hover within a range of 1.2633-1.2688, with inclination toward the topside due to broad U.S. dollar strength. Weakness in global equity markets, though mild so far, is creating an air of caution and prompting traders to be less bullish on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in general. Recently poor economic data from China may also affect investors' views for the trade-dependent Singapore economy; Wednesday's China trade data could be the next catalyst for USD/SGD. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2633 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 1.2600 (psychological support), before 1.2581 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2688 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2700 (psychological resistance), before 1.2742 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--consolidation. USD/MYR could drift within a range of 3.2710-3.3000 as the U.S. dollar stays firm due to mild risk aversion while the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  near 3.3000 deters traders from betting against the ringgit. Market chatter of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank Negara on Friday continues to haunt traders who suspect that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is drawing a line in the sand for ringgit weakness and will act to defend that level if tested again. But if the U.S. dollar index resumes its rally and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciate further against the greenback, the Malaysia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could step away from defending 3.3000 and allow the ringgit to weaken again in line with regionals. On the sidelines, protests by religious groups and by media journalists for more press freedom could cast a shadow on the otherwise improving economic fundamentals. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2800 (psychological support), then at 3.2710 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 3.2500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 3.2950 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.3000 (major psychological resistance), before 3.3200 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--upside bias. The baht is still on a weak footing even as the scheduled Feb. 2 election is on track. USD/THB is still within the Bollinger uptrend channel and above the psychological support of 33.00, indicating traders are still bearish on the baht. The political crisis may soon worsen as protesters carry out more frequent rallies ahead of a planned large-scale occupation of undisclosed sites on Jan. 13. The baht's collapse shows little sign of stopping, after hitting yet another nearly 4-year low of 33.13 on Monday. Already down 6.3% since late October when the amnesty bill was proposed by Prime Minister Yingluck to pave the way for her brother Thaksin's return, there could be more room for the baht to fall. The threat of more rallies and a shutdown of key infrastructure and services is now threatening tourism--one of the nation's key economic engines of growth. USD/THB may soon rise to the top of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 33.17. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 33.00 (psychological support), then at 32.80 (psychological support), before 32.62 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 33.13 (4-year high), then at 33.17 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 33.20 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation with upside bias. USD/PHP could stabilize for now after having hit a 4-month high of 44.75 on Monday as the lead indicator U.S. dollar index subsided overnight. The peso has been losing ground to the dollar alongside other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors become more bullish for the U.S. economy and thereby the dollar. As the U.S. economy improves, the U.S. Federal Reserve could sooner reduce bond-buying again--which would elevate the benchmark U.S. bond yields and boost the dollar by proxy. If USD/PHP rises above 44.75, the first time since Sep. 2010, a new 3.5-year high could be recorded. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.50 (psychological support), then at 44.26 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.74 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 44.75 (4-month high), before 44.80 (psychological resistance)\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--consolidation with upside bias. USD/IDR may linger at the base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel as the U.S. dollar index subsided overnight. The technical upside bias could however remain as long as the dollar stays above 12,150 by the end of the day. There is broad bullishness for the dollar this year due to signs that the U.S. economy is improving to the point that less support from the U.S. Federal Reserve is necessary. If the Fed takes another step to remove its bond-buying stimulus measures, the dollar will likely spike again. Most analysts think the rupiah is most susceptible to weakness if the Fed reduces its bond-buying program--which could lead to an exodus of foreign funds that have invested in Indonesian assets since U.S. quantitative easing began in 2008. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 12,150 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 12,000 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 12,278 (5-year high), then at 12,300 (psychological resistance), before 12,480 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 6 Jan 2014 19:54 EDT  USD/Asia Bullish as U.S. Stocks Slip -- Asia -2-\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation, possible upside bias. The Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone has so far managed to keep the dollar from rallying much higher, thus buffering the rupee from more losses. A slight dip in the U.S. dollar index overnight could help to keep the Cloud resistance zone intact. But if investors' risk appetite worsens again and the dollar rises above 62.49, the breach of the Cloud would pave the way for further dollar strength. The macro focus for India investors in 2014 will be the general elections in April-May; though the general consensus is that an opposition-led government would be more business-friendly and thereby a boon for the rupee, some analysts have tempered expectations for short term improvement in economic growth. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 62.14 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 62.00 (psychological support), before 61.80 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 62.41 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 62.49 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 62.70 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does no