\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Up as Dollar Index Spikes Again -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,744 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2014\par 01:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0500-6.0570   6.0400-6.0600 \par USD/TWD   29.880-30.000   29.800-30.070 \par USD/KRW    1,055-1,060     1,052-1,063 \par USD/SGD   1.2623-1.2685   1.2600-1.2700 \par USD/MYR   3.2800-3.2950   3.2670-3.3000 \par USD/THB    33.00-33.12     32.80-33.20 \par USD/PHP    44.50-44.69     44.22-44.75 \par USD/IDR   12,150-12,278   12,000-12,300 \par USD/INR    62.12-62.41     62.00-62.68 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation higher. New record highs for the yuan are unlikely for now as the overnight surge in the U.S. dollar index--the second in as many days--implies the PBOC will set the benchmark USD/CNY parity rate higher again, possibly nearer to 6.1100 from Friday's 6.1039. The jump in the U.S. dollar index came about due to a significantly weaker euro. China stocks may still be under the weather as the Shanghai Composite Index failed to break out of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel on Friday, suggesting more downside may resume this week. China's official services PMI will be released later today at 0145 GMT. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.0500 (record low and psychological support), before 6.0400 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.0570 (lower Bollinger band standard deviation 2), then at 6.0600 (psychological resistance), before 6.0700 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--upside bias. USD/TWD has resumed its bullish technical bias on the daily chart and may soon reach the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 30.070. The price difference between the 1-month USD/TWD non-deliverable forward contract and the spot price turned positive on Friday, a sign that offshore traders are getting more bullish on the dollar. The dollar is likely to stay strong as Asia traders start to get spooked by the recent steep rise of the U.S. dollar index-- which could persuade them to reduce their short-USD bets. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.880 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 29.800 (psychological support), before 29.690 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.000 (psychological resistance), before 30.070 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation higher. USD/KRW has risen above the 20-day Bollinger mid and thus entered an elevated consolidation range of 1,055-1,060. The biddish tone in USD/KRW follows a second consecutive rise in the U.S. dollar index. Another reason keeping USD/KRW well-supported is market chatter of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2 --after the won touched a new 5-year high against the Japanese yen last Thursday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  occasionally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market to ensure exchange rate-related price competitiveness for local exporters versus Japanese rivals. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,055 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 1,052 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,050 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1,060 (psychological resistance and daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,063 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel and Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation. USD/SGD appears to be lacking momentum to trade much higher, judging by the failed attempt Friday to enter the Bollinger uptrend channel which now caps at 1.2685. Until the Bollinger uptrend channel comes into play, USD/SGD is likely to hover within a range of 1.2623-1.2685, with inclination toward the higher end of this range due to broad U.S. dollar strength. Traders are getting more bullish on the greenback in general following a second consecutive sharp fall in the euro late last week. The rise of the dollar is creating a mild risk aversion in Asia that could weigh on most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2623 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 1.2600 (psychological support), before 1.2561 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2685 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2700 (psychological resistance), before 1.2746 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--possible upside bias. USD/MYR may shy away from 3.3000 after market chatter of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank Negara on Friday to stem ringgit weakness at that level. The dollar, though higher on a broad basis after Friday's sharp drop in the euro, could hence consolidate for now at current levels. But if the U.S. dollar index continues to rise and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciate further against the greenback, the Malaysia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could step away from defending 3.3000 and allow the ringgit to weaken again in line with regionals. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2800 (psychological support), then at 3.2670 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 3.2500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 3.2950 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.3000 (major psychological resistance), before 3.3230 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--upside bias. The baht is likely to weaken as the political crisis deepens with protesters planning more frequent rallies and organising a large-scale occupation of undisclosed sites on Jan. 13 to disrupt the election process. The baht fell to a nearly 4-year low of 33.03 on Friday as investors brace for a potential full-blown political crisis. The threat of more rallies and a shutdown of key infrastructure and services is also threatening tourism--one of the nation's key economic engines of growth. USD/THB may soon rise to the top of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 33.12. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 33.00 (psychological support), then at 32.80 (psychological support), before 32.57 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 33.03 (4-year high), then at 33.12 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 33.20 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--upside bias. More upside appears likely for USD/PHP after the dollar ended Friday near its 4-month high--an indication that upside momentum is strong. The second consecutive overnight spike in the U.S. dollar index is likely to drive USD/PHP toward the previous peak of 44.75 seen in August. The U.S. dollar is broadly stronger Monday, despite the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury yield slipping back under the psychological barrier of 3.0%, due to another sharp drop in the euro on Friday. Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders often look to the euro for a leading sign of dollar sentiment, and are likely to get spooked by the euro's tumble on Thursday. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.50 (psychological support), then at 44.22 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.69 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel),then at 44.75 (4-month high), before 44.80 (psychological resistance)\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. As the U.S dollar index rises again, USD/IDR is likely to head back above 12,200. Friday's failed attempt to breach the base of the Bollinger uptrend channel suggests buying of the dollar on dips is prevalent. As long as the Bollinger uptrend channel continues to support at 12,150, the technical bias for more rupiah weakness will persist. Most analysts think the rupiah is susceptible to weakness as the U.S. Federal Reserve withdraws its bond-buying program which could lead to an exodus of foreign funds that have invested in Indonesian assets since U.S. quantitative easing began in 2008. Indonesia's December Manufacturing PMI released last Friday rose to 50.9 versus the previous score of 50.3, which may have helped shore up rupiah weakness. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 12,150 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 12,000 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 12,278 (5-year high), then at 12,300 (psychological resistance), before 12,480 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--possible upside bias. As the U.S. dollar rises broadly in Asia following the steep fall in the euro on Friday, USD/INR could make another attempt to rally above the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone that caps at 62.49. A daily closing above the Cloud would pave the way for further dollar strength versus the rupee. Disappointing India HSBC Manufacturing PMI for December released on Thursday provides a bearish backdrop for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The key indicator of growth in the manufacturing sector appears particularly negative for the rupee because other manufacturing PMIs released in Asia last week were upbeat. The macro focus for India investors in 2014 will be the general elections in April-May; though the general consensus is that an opposition-led government would be more business-friendly and thereby a boon for the rupee, some analysts have tempered expectations for short term improvement in economic growth. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 62.12 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 62.00 (psychological support), before 61.80 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 62.41 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 62.49 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 62.68 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 05, 2014 19:50 ET (00:50 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140106ea160003d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
