\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 South Korea \highlight\uc2 's Won Falls After Officials Hint of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anjani Trivedi   \par \uc2 660 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2014\par 18:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won fell against the dollar and yen after officials there hinted they were ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.\par \par \uc2 The remarks from two South Korean finance officials came after the won hit a two-year high against the dollar last week and reached a five-year high against the yen on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The exchange rate between the two Asian countries is closely watched, as they compete head-to-head around the world to sell everything from smartphones to cars. The won's 16% rise against the yen since June has come as Tokyo has sought to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help kick-start the Japanese economy.\par \par \uc2 The pain is also spilling over to the stock market. South Korea's benchmark index ended Friday at a four-month low, and technology giant \uc2 Samsung Electronics Co\uc2 . was down 5.5% this week in part because of fears the won's strength will hurt its profits.\par \par \uc2 "We will strengthen our monitoring for offshore flows and when needed carry out stabilizing measures for financial and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," said Bank of Korea Gov. Kim Choong-soo in an address to financial institutions Friday.\par \par \uc2 Those comments came on the same day that South Korea's finance minister, Hyun Oh-seok, said in a separate meeting with banking executives that the country is "monitoring the market flows," adding that "we musn't be agitated by every positive or negative movement."\par \par \uc2 In South Korea, the finance ministry directs \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acts on its behalf.\par \par \uc2 The comments helped push the won lower Friday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened 0.5% to 1055.0 won to the dollar, and was off 0.8% to 10.100 won against the yen.\par \par \uc2 While the \uc2 South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to help smooth volatility, and in October bought some $2 billion to slow gains, the comments Friday indicated an increase in concern.\par \par \uc2 The won's strength stands South Korea in contrast to many other emerging economies, where steep slides in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates have become a point of concern for policy makers.\par \par \uc2 Central banks in Turkey and Brazil have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and Indian policy makers last year took a variety of steps to shore up the Indian rupee after it hit record lows. Those \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dived for much of 2013 on concerns the Federal Reserve was looking to reduce the stimulus efforts that had helped drive investors to emerging-market assets for years. Excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness can exacerbate inflation and put central banks under pressure to raise interest rates at a time when many emerging economies are struggling to grow faster.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect Samsung to report a drop in operating profit when the company reports quarterly earnings on Tuesday in part because the strong won has driven up expenses, particularly in its components and display businesses, where manufacturing costs are concentrated domestically.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Samsung Electronics Co\uc2 . is paying close attention to global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trends and is responding to (potential) \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks by diversifying its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  portfolio," a company spokeswoman said, without elaborating.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the won is unlikely to give up ground soon. \uc2 Credit Agricole SA\uc2  expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will strengthen further against both the dollar and yen in 2014, forecasting that it could reach 8.87 won against the yen by December.\par \par \uc2 Some manufacturers can benefit from a strong won because it makes imported components cheaper, said Frances Cheung, head of Asian rates strategy at \uc2 Cr\u233\'00\'E9dit Agricole\uc2 . But while South Korean goods are still cheaper overall, "a strong KRW [won] will undermine the pricing ability of Korean entities," she said.\par \par \uc2 -- Erin McCarthy, Jeyup Kwaak and Min-Jeong Lee contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Anjani Trivedi at anjani.trivedi@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 03, 2014 12:41 ET (17:41 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140103ea13001xv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
