\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Up As Fed Fears Return -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,994 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 2013\par 01:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0704-6.0800   6.0700-6.0833 \par USD/TWD   29.560-29.650   29.500-29.710 \par USD/KRW    1,051-1,055     1,050-1,058 \par USD/SGD   1.2549-1.2574   1.2513-1.2600 \par USD/MYR   3.2310-3.2480   3.2280-3.2500 \par USD/THB    32.00-32.20     31.97-32.37 \par USD/PHP    44.00-44.17     43.88-44.35 \par USD/IDR   12,000-12,100   11,900-12,200 \par USD/INR    61.50-61.87     61.34-62.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation higher. The overnight rebound in the U.S. dollar index is a leading indicator for a higher USD/CNY central parity rate--which is determined by the PBOC based on what it deems is an appropriate relative value for the yuan. A higher USD/CNY yuan parity rate would propel spot USD/CNY off the base of the Bollinger downtrend channel and toward the top of the channel at 6.0833. There are likely to be plenty of sellers lurking at higher levels in USD/CNY as traders are looking for opportunities to buy the yuan at cheaper levels with the view that the authorities are speeding up financial reforms that may see the yuan gain more sharply in the medium term. The yuan is by far the best performer in Asia this year--up as much as 2.7% when it hit its 2013 peak on Tuesday. The Chinese authorities have been allowing a stronger yuan--partly because a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will help boost domestic consumption but also because it is another step toward the eventual liberalization of the yuan which many believe to be undervalued. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.0704 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.0703 (record low), then at 6.0700 (psychological support), before 6.0600 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.0800 (psychological resistance), then at 6.0833 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation. USD/TWD is likely to continue trading sideways as the pair lacks momentum on the charts to break away higher or lower. The dollar has been stable, likely because of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and thus has deterred speculators from betting on the Taiwan dollar, which reduces its volatility even further. \uc2 Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one of the most active in influencing the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the open market, often buying and selling within the same day to maneuver USD/TWD within an acceptable range. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may allow the Taiwan dollar to fall against the greenback Friday--which is helpful to Taiwanese exporters--after the dollar rose broadly overnight. Fear of a possible U.S. Federal Reserve reduction in bond buying at the Dec. 17-18 Fed policy meeting is once again lifting the dollar. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.560 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 29.500 (psychological support), before 29.470 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is likely at 29.650 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 29.710 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 29.730 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation higher. USD/KRW rebounds away from the base of the Bollinger downtrend channel and further away from the two-year low notched on Wednesday as the U.S. dollar rallies broadly on speculation that the U.S. Federal Reserve may announce a reduction in bond buying next week. The fear of a withdrawal of monetary stimulus sent stocks down for a third day in the U.S. and will likely have a similar impact in Asia. As investors turn more cautious on the weakness in stocks, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders are trimming 'risk-on' positions such as being long the \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  won. Traders aware of possible Bank of Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  near the psychological support of 1,050 might be another factor that will keep USD/KRW well-bid. \uc2 The Bank of Korea\uc2  kept its benchmark interest rates unchanged on Thursday. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,051 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,050 (psychological support), before 1,040 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1,055 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,058 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 1,060 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--uptrend returns. USD/SGD has climbed back inside the Bollinger uptrend channel--a bullish signal--and may now target a break of the Ichimoku Cloud resistance at 1.2574. If USD/SGD ends Friday above this level, the charts would turn even more bullish for the greenback. The overnight rally in the dollar, which was accompanied by third consecutive selloff in U.S. stocks, was likely owing to anxiety that the U.S. Federal Reserve may surprise markets by announcing a reduction in bond buying at the Dec. 17-18 Fed policy meeting. USD/SGD is likely to be well-supported by the base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 1.2549 and dealers may be motivated to push the dollar higher later in the day--when liquidity is reduced and punters get more anxious to close out short-USD positions before the weekend--to trigger stop-loss orders lurking above the psychological trading barrier at 1.2600. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2549 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2513 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 1.2500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2574 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 1.2585 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2600 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--upside bias. USD/MYR is on a path toward 3.2500 now that the dollar has risen above the entire Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and is now also in the Bollinger uptrend channel, signs of increased momentum for a bigger move up. The dollar rose overnight as speculators sold off risk assets such as stocks and emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the perceived safety of the U.S. dollar. Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are broadly lower following a third decline in U.S. stocks overnight that signals investors are getting more cautious ahead of next week's U.S. Federal Reserve policy meeting that may result in a reduction of bond buying. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2310 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2280 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 3.2170 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 3.2480 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation higher. USD/THB is now more likely to rise back to the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel as the dollar rises broadly following another round of selloff in risk assets overnight. Already under pressure owing to continuing political unrest in Bangkok, where protesters on Thursday cut power and water to the government headquarters, the baht may also weaken on fear that the U.S. Federal Reserve may next week announce a reduction in bond buying. The next target for USD/THB would be the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 32.38, which is just above the 3-month peak of 32.37 notched last week. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.00 (psychological support), then at 31.97 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 31.80 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 32.20 (psychological resistance), then at 32.37 (3-month high), before 32.38 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--upside bias. The sharp rebound in the U.S. dollar index overnight and the continuing bullish technical bias for USD/PHP will help pull the greenback toward the 3-month high of 44.35 touched on Tuesday. The \uc2 Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday kept its benchmark interest rate at its record low, which was expected, citing low inflation. The focus for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders is still the U.S. Federal Reserve policy meeting next week--which may result in a reduction of bond buying by the Fed. Risk aversion recently has triggered big outflows from offshore hedge funds in equities as well as away from bullish bets on the peso, said one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer based in Manila. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.00 (psychological support), before 43.88 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.17 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 44.35 (3-month high), before 44.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. USD/IDR may surpass the near 5-year high of 12,040 notched on Thursday as the U.S. dollar rises again on escalating risk aversion ahead of next week's U.S. Federal Reserve policy meeting. The Indonesia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  yesterday decided to keep the benchmark rate unchanged, as expected, and said it would strengthen its policy responses if the Fed starts reducing bond buying. The comments from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  affirms analysts' view that central banks in Asia are generally waiting for the Fed to signal its willingness to reduce monetary stimulus before they react. \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  would have to react quickly in the event of the Fed withdrawing stimulus, as the rupiah is one of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  most susceptible to outflows, analysts believe. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 12,000 (psychological support), then at 11,900 (psychological support), before 11,820 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 12,100 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 12,200 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 12 Dec 2013 19:55 EDT  USD/Asia Up As Fed Fears Return -- Asia Daily -2-\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--possible upside bias. USD/INR may take on a more bullish bias if it rises above the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance at 61.98. The U.S. dollar is stronger across the board as risk aversion escalates, as seen in the third decline in U.S. stocks overnight. As the U.S. Federal Reserve policy meeting next week draws closer, investors are getting more jittery and selling off risk assets for the perceived safety of the U.S. dollar. Adding to U.S. dollar bullishness, the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield has also been on the rise as investors anticipate a possible reduction in bond buying by the Fed. The recent euphoria for the rupee following the state election results, where the opposition party won important victories, has since fizzled out as the market focuses on event risks closer on the horizon, such as the possibility of the Fed reducing bond buying. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 61.50 (psychological support), then at 61.34 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 61.00 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 61.87 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 61.89 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 62.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 12, 2013 19:55 ET (00:55 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131213e9cd0007k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
