\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Bullish Technical Signals Abound -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,825 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2013\par 01:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0907-6.1000   6.0900-6.1046 \par USD/TWD   29.570-29.680   29.500-29.710 \par USD/KRW    1,060-1,063     1,058-1,067 \par USD/SGD   1.2481-1.2519   1.2446-1.2546 \par USD/MYR   3.2000-3.2260   3.1800-3.2390 \par USD/THB    31.67-31.80     31.52-32.00 \par USD/PHP    43.65-43.80     43.55-43.89 \par USD/IDR   11,560-11,710   11,500-11,800 \par USD/INR    62.83-63.00     62.50-63.51 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. The PBOC daily benchmark rate for USD/CNY could be set higher in line with the rise in USD/JPY above 101.00. The weaker yen has an influence on the value of the Chinese yuan. The charts suggest USD/CNY has lost its bearish technical bias now that the pair is no longer inside the daily Bollinger downtrend channel. Thursday's escape from the channel could indicate a firmer dollar toward 6.1000 today. The HSBC China Flash Manufacturing PMI for November, released Thursday, was mildly disappointing at 50.4 versus the previous reading of 50.9. Though this did not affect Chinese stocks very much, it weakened the Australia dollar and some Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.0907 (entrance of Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.0900 (psychological support), before 6.0802 (record low). Immediate resistance is at 6.1000 (psychological resistance), before 6.1046 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation higher. USD/TWD has a mild bullish bias now that the dollar has climbed above the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance line at 29.570. The dollar's rally against the Japanese yen, which hit a 4-month high due to stoploss orders triggered, may be leading the charge higher for the rest of Asia. Investors are still looking for signs that the U.S. Federal Reserve could reduce monetary stimulus in the months ahead; mixed economic data recently has made forecasts more difficult. A strong showing in U.S. stocks overnight, which saw the Dow Jones Industrial Average hit a new all-time high, could however promote investor sentiment that might help to buffer Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from further selloffs. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.570 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 29.500 (psychological support and base of Ichimoku Cloud), before 29.460 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 29.680 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 29.710 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation with upside bias. The dollar could take on a more bullish bias if it ends Friday above 1,063--the 20-day Bollinger mid that now acts a technical resistance. Broad dollar strength due to expectations of an impending reduction of monetary stimulus by the U.S. Federal Reserve has been fuelling USD/Asia higher in general. Another factor which could spur USD/KRW higher is the steep rise of USD/JPY overnight. Yen weakness is typically followed by weakness for the \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  won as \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market to ensure that the won retains its relative value to the yen--which gives South Korea exporters a competitive advantage. USD/KRW appears firm ahead of the 1,060 psychological support, but has struggled to rally for now due to exporters selling near 1,063, said a trader. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,060 (psychological support), then at 1,058 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,053 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,063 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 1,067 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--upside bias. USD/SGD is likely to be drawn higher by the Bollinger uptrend channel that came into effect Thursday. The technical signal suggest the greenback will be supported at 1.2481 and could rise as high as 1.2517 before abating. The steep rise of USD/JPY may be playing a part in guiding USD/SGD higher, said a trader, due to the proxy effect the weaker yen has on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that are managed by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  via relative trade value. USD/SGD may appear even more bullish if it ends Friday above 1.2546, which would place it above the weekly Ichimoku Cloud--an additional bullish technical signal for the medium term. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2481 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2446 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 1.2410 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2519 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2546 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--upside bias. The bullish technical bias gains momentum as USD/MYR moves higher into the Bollinger uptrend channel that came into effect Thursday. The next target for the dollar could be 3.2260 which is the top of the uptrend channel. The dollar rose sharply against the Japanese yen to hit a 4-month high, triggering most USD/Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs higher as well. The strong showing in U.S. equity markets overnight is however giving Asia stocks a lift, which may help to slow the weakening of Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2000 (psychological barrier, and base of Ichimoku Cloud, and bottom of Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.1800 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 3.2260 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2390 (top of Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--upside bias. The path toward 32.00 has gotten a boost from the big overnight move in USD/JPY, which is pulling most USD/Asia upwards as well. The charts are looking bullish for USD/THB now that the dollar is well above the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and also in the weekly Bollinger uptrend channel that suggests more dollar strength in the medium term. The greenback has been on the rise since the U.S. FOMC minutes revealed that tapering of monetary stimulus could still happen in the coming months. Some traders have been shorting the Thai baht in anticipation of more weakness, due to domestic political concerns and slowing economic growth. The National Economic and Social Development Board earlier this week revised down its full-year growth projection to 3.0% from 3.8%-4.3%. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 31.67 (Ichimoku Cloud support zone), then at 31.52 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel ), before 31.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 31.80 (psychological resistance), before 32.00 (psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--possible bullish signal appearing. USD/PHP has a high chance of breaking through the top of the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone at 43.89--which would suggest even more dollar upside in the near term. The dollar is rising across Asia Friday, driven by the proxy effect of the USD/JPY rally, and also bullish-dollar technical signals appearing against various Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Onshore oil importers have been consistently strong buyers of the dollar this week, said a trader, adding to dollar biddishness that may be spooking the speculative short positions. These punters, who have typically short-term positions and therefore balk easily at moves against their favor, may likely soon buy back their dollars and thereby add to USD/PHP upside momentum. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.65 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel) , then at 43.55 (base of Ichimoku Cloud), before 43.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.80 (psychological resistance), then at 43.89 (top of Ichimoku Cloud), before 43.94 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. The rupiah, which fell to a 4.5-year low of 11,725 against the dollar Thursday, may weaken further as the dollar rises across the board. The steep rally in USD/JPY has led most USD/Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs higher and the likelihood of the U.S. Federal Reserve reducing monetary stimulus has been an underlying factor for dollar strength. Adding to the USD/IDR bullish view is the dimming prospect for the Indonesia economy which has been further hampered by last week's surprise interest rate hike by \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 . Ratings agency Fitch this week lowered its growth forecast for next year's Gross Domestic Product to 5.3% from 5.5% in 2013. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,560 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 11,500 (psychological support), before 11,410 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support and 20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 11,710 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 11,800 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--upside bias. A bullish USD/INR technical signal has emerged after the dollar ended Thursday above 62.83--the entrance of the Bollinger uptrend channel. The dollar has been rallying broadly across Asia, particularly after the mildly hawkish tone revealed in the U.S. FOMC minutes. The rupee could weaken to 63.5--the top of the USD/INR uptrend channel - though \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  might slow the move, said a trader. The RBI was suspected to have been selling dollars in the spot market Thursday near the 63.00 psychological barrier, possibly aware that stoploss orders above that level could trigger a sudden slide for the rupee. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 62.83 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 62.50 (psychological support), before 62.15 (20-day Bollinger mid support and base of Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is likely at 63.00 (psychological trading barrier), then at 63.51 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 64.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 21 Nov 2013 19:52 EDT  USD/Asia Bullish Technical Signals Abound -- Asia -2-\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 21, 2013 19:52 ET (00:52 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131122e9bm00077\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
