\par\par \b \uc2 USD/KRW Spikes To 1,062 On Fear Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 151 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2013\par 07:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Korean (English)\par \uc2 RTNWK\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0545 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  won slumped rapidly on fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  said it is monitoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, concerned about volatility, and will take action if necessary. This form of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , construed by market participants as the BOK's warning to punters to avoid speculating on the won, sent USD/KRW soaring to 1,062 from 1,055 within minutes in a wave of panicked USD-short covering. The move implies a 0.7% depreciation of the won. The USD/KRW has now settled slightly lower at 1,059.0. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 24, 2013 01:45 ET (05:45 GMT)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 24-10-13 0555GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNWK00020131024e9ao0000g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
