\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar Ekes Gains Versus Most Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan   \par \uc2 446 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2013\par 17:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar is gaining momentum against many emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained beyond its reach Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose 0.7% to the Brazilian real at BRL2.2037, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 After eking steady gains the real seems to be losing steam and inching above BRL2.20 to the dollar on global factors that are boosting the dollar, including concerns about some European financial institutions.\par \par \uc2 However, many Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  broke off from that trend due to the better-than-expected, preliminary manufacturing data from China that came in at 50.9 versus expectations of 50.4. Their gains, however, were muted by concerns that \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be tightening its monetary system and reducing liquidity. Short-term rates in China jumped across various maturities.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose 0.3% to the Malaysian ringgit to trade at MYR3.1559, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 Overnight, the Philippines \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held rates, as expected, at 3.5%. The country's inflation remained under control with the bank predicting an annual rise of 3% in prices. \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  expects more support if the Philippine peso strengthens below PHP43 to the dollar. It currently trades at PHP43.08.\par \par \uc2 South Africa also benefited from expectations of improved demand from China. The dollar weakened 0.33% to the rand at ZAR9.76. Still, concerns persist in the country, said Razia Khan, strategist with Standard Chartered Bank.\par \par \uc2 Even though South Africa cut it's official growth rate forecast to 2.1%, it wasn't seen as a worrisome development as it matched existing market consensus, she said.\par \par \uc2 The country, however, has seen a rise in flows into its local bond markets driven by increased investor comfort with the stability of the rand and the draw of the country's higher yields.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  led the won to weaken. \uc2 The Bank of Korea\uc2  said it is monitoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, concerned about volatility, and will take action if necessary. This form of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , construed by market participants as the BOK's warning to punters to avoid speculating on the won, pushed the dollar up to KRW1061.7, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in the debt markets, issuers continued to use the window of opportunity to raise money. \uc2 Turkiye Vakiflar Bankasi\uc2  plans to raise $500 million of five-year unsecured debt. The deal is expected to price later in the day.\par \par \uc2 -- Ewen Chew contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Prabha Natarajan at prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 24, 2013 11:00 ET (15:00 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131024e9ao003hd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
