\par\par \b \uc2 Stress Tests Will Be Key For ECB Too--Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,430 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2013\par 09:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0700 GMT [Dow Jones]--European markets got the vapors late Wednesday as investors looked ahead to forthcoming stress tests of large European lenders by the ECB. However, this round of assessments could also be crucial for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  itself. There have been two previous rounds of tests in recent years, neither of which garnered the full faith and confidence of the markets. The latest will need to be robust, and calibrated for worse scenarios than their predecessors. (david.cottle@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0632 GMT [Dow Jones] The EUR/USD breaks above the 1.3800 mark for the first time since November 2011, with options linked stop-loss purchase sending it as high as 1.3817, says a senior dealer at a Japanese bank."Amid the dollar's across-the-board weakness, the euro has apparently been chosen by investors as an alternative for the dollar," he adds. The pair is recently at 1.3811. "Since the euro broke through the key 1.3800, there is no major resistance until 1.4000," which was last hit back in October 31, 2011, he adds. (tatsuo.ito@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0614 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP has been stable Thursday ahead of the 0800GMT release of the Philippines \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest-rate decision. The dollar has bobbed within a narrow range of 43.08-43.16 so far, as the market expects no change to the benchmark lending rate. But the peso could be poised to appreciate if USD/PHP ends the day below 43.10 and therefore inside the daily Bollinger downtrend channel. Upon confirmation of the downtrend bias, USD/PHP could target the base of the channel at 42.56. Analysts think that \uc2 Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas\uc2  has no need to adjust its interest-rate policy because of benign inflation and a robust economy. USD/PHP is now 43.10. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0600 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/INR seems to be caught in a psychological trading range between 61.00-62.00 for now, but with growing hopes of fiscal and banking sector reform, the USD/INR could break lower in the medium term. The push by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's governor \uc2 Raghuram Rajan\uc2  to revamp the financial sector - which would ease foreign banks' entry - is improving the outlook for foreign inflows and therefore the rupee. At the Institute of International Finance in Washington earlier this month, Mr. Rajan laid out his five pillars for financial reform, including a clearer monetary policy framework. Additionally, India's likely inclusion into the \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  global bond index could help boost inflows, possibly by as much as $40 billion. These ongoing developments could be enough to encourage opportunistic bets on rupee strength in the near future. The USD/INR is now 61.46. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0558 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/JPY is edging higher as the benchmark Nikkei stock index has turned positive, improving risk sentiment, says a Japanese bank dealer. The pair is at 97.59 after it fell earlier to as low as 97.17. "The pair is finding support at the 200-days moving average of around 97.30," he says. But the pair may come under selling pressure from Japanese exporters which apparently lowered their offers from the previous 99 level, he adds.(tatsuo.ito@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0545 GMT [Dow Jones] The \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  won slumped rapidly on fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  said it is monitoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, concerned about volatility, and will take action if necessary. This form of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , construed by market participants as the BOK's warning to punters to avoid speculating on the won, sent USD/KRW soaring to 1,062 from 1,055 within minutes in a wave of panicked USD-short covering. The move implies a 0.7% depreciation of the won. The USD/KRW has now settled slightly lower at 1,059.0. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0545 GMT [Dow Jones] The \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  won slumped rapidly on fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  said it is monitoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, concerned about volatility, and will take action if necessary. This form of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , construed by market participants as the BOK's warning to punters to avoid speculating on the won, sent USD/KRW soaring to 1,062 from 1,055 within minutes in a wave of panicked USD-short covering. The move implies a 0.7% depreciation of the won. The USD/KRW has now settled slightly lower at 1,059.0. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0515 GMT [Dow Jones] The NZD/USD has "popped higher" following a narrower than expected local trade deficit and upbeat Chinese data, although much of the gains have now disappeared as focus returns to the USD story, says \uc2 HiFX\uc2  Head of Trading Alex Hill. The pair is at 0.8412 vs. 0.8377 early this morning. Statistics NZ earlier said the September trade deficit was just NZ$199 million vs. market expectation of a NZ$800 million deficit, while the initial October HSBC China's manufacturing activity came out at 50.9 vs. a final reading of 50.2 in September. Hill puts support for the pair at 0.8380 with resistance coming at 0.8520. (lucy.craymer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0507 GMT [Dow Jones] As the weekend approaches, certainty is rising for a medium-term bearish signal for USD/SGD on the weekly chart. On a Friday close below 1.2380, the USD/SGD would be beneath the Ichimoku Cloud support zone and also inside the Bollinger downtrend channel. The significance of the dollar falling below the Cloud support is increased by the Chikou line--a momentum indicator that is current price action overlayed 26 periods backwards--also dropping below the Cloud support. The additional bearish technical indicator of the Bollinger downtrend channel, which has already been in play since 5 weeks ago, adds to conviction that USD/SGD could fall to its May low of 1.2261 in weeks to come. USD/SGD is now 1.2368. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0447 GMT [Dow Jones] Though today's U.S. intial jobless claims report will be tainted by effects of the two-week partial government shutdown, it may still create volatility in markets when it is released later. Economists will attempt to strip out the effects of claims by government workers, and then arrive at a more accurate private sector unemployment picture. Steady job creation is one of the main variables which will influence when the Federal Reserve tapers its monetary stimulus - a key event risk to financial markets. The week before, U.S. intial jobless claims dropped 15,000 to 358,000. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0340 GMT [Dow Jones] Standard Chartered revises up its forecast for China's gross domestic product growth for 2013 to 7.6% from 7.5%. It revises its forecast for 2014 to 7.4% from 7.2%. A number of indicators suggests an improvement in broad-based growth in the third quarter and momentum should continue, it says in a research note. Economic growth expanded 7.8% on year in the third quarter--up from 7.5% in the second quarter. Standard Chartered raises its CPI forecast to 2.7% for this year from 2.5% and to 3.3% for 2014 from 3.0%. (grace.zhu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0339 GMT [Dow Jones] China shares are lower midday, extending Wednesday's losses, as investors continue to desert cyclical shares amid uncertainties over economic outlook, analysts say. The Shanghai Composite Index falls 0.2% to 2177.90 and may find its immediate support at 2150. "The chances for a strong market after the conclusion of a key party meeting in November do not look very good," HFT Investment Management says in a research note, citing that the domestic economy is unlikely to post a marked rise in 4Q due to high base effect. Among actives, cyclical shares are lower with Yanzhou Coal Mining (600188.SH) down 2.3% at CNY10.99, metal firm Chalco (601600.SH) off 2.1% at CNY4.18 and \uc2 Baoshan Iron & Steel\uc2  (600019.SH) losing 1.2% to CNY4.11. The Shenzhen Composite Index is flat at 1065.34. (amy.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 24, 2013 03:00 ET (07:00 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131024e9ao000yj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
