\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves hit new high in July,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen\b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2013\par 23:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Aug 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves jumped to a record high in July, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday, appearing to support traders' suspicions of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities last month. The reserves stood at $329.71 billion at the end of July, up $3.27 billion from June, \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  said in a statement, attributing the rise to management gains and the appreciation of the euro in July, which \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  said was up 1.8 percent against the dollar last month. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It does not give a breakdown of the reserves by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  engages in what it calls market-smoothing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 activities to reduce fluctuation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but it does not disclose or confirm the details of its actions. A \uc2 Bank of Korea\uc2  official declined to comment on the market talk regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The won rose 1.6 percent against the dollar in July, despite tremors throughout emerging markets as investors speculated over the timing of the U.S. Federal Reserve's tapering of its bond-buying stimulus. South Korea had the seventh-largest foreign reserves as of the end of June, 91.4 percent of which was in the form of securities.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     South Korean foreign reserves (in $ bln, at end-month):\par  Jul      Jun      May      Apr      Mar      Feb      Jan\par  329.71   326.44   328.10   328.80   327.41   327.40   328.91\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Christine Kim; Editing by Eric Meijer)\f28 \par \par \uc2 KOREA-ECONOMY/RESERVES (URGENT) | ABX | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130804e984000a3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
