\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 551 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2013\par 09:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Japan's Aso Rules Out \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  For Now\par \par \uc2 Japan's finance minister said he has no intention to order direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to tackle the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent rebound, in a rare move for a Japanese official to publicly rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a sharp appreciation.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's GDP Grows 0.8%\par \par \uc2 The South Korean economy improved in the first quarter from the prior three months, but at a slightly slower pace than previously forecast.\par \par \uc2 North Korea Will Resume Hotline With South\par \par \uc2 North Korea has suggested it is prepared to reinstate communication channels, Korean Central News Agency said. They were largely cut off by the North earlier this year following the imposition of sanctions on the North for its Feb. 12 nuclear test.\par \par \uc2 ECB Rules Out Stimulus, Despite Poorer Outlook\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took no new steps to boost the euro zone's flagging economic prospects despite forecasting an even-deeper recession this year and low inflation in 2014, putting its stimulus tools "on the shelf."\par \par \uc2 Soros Fund Back in Japan Market\par \par \uc2 Investors of all types are selling Japanese stocks, worried a recovery might not be easy for the government to engineer. But \uc2 George Soros\uc2 's firm, \uc2 Soros Fund Management\uc2 , is buying once again [ 07-06-13 0705GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Bundesbank Lowers Germany's Growth Forecast\par \par \uc2 Germany's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its growth forecast for Europe's largest economy this year and next, tying the nation's fate to whether the euro-zone emerges from recession.\par \par \uc2 EU's Rehn Slams IMF over Greece\par \par \uc2 European Union\uc2  Economics Chief Olli Rehn had harsh words for the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  Friday as he responded to a report by the IMF criticizing the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  over the Greek bailout.\par \par \uc2 Italy Credit Crunch Heats Up\par \par \uc2 Italian bank loans to companies fell 3.7% in April from the same month a year earlier, the fastest decline seen during the country's current recession, the \uc2 Bank of Italy\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Japan's Aso Rules Out \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  For Now\par \par \uc2 Japan's finance minister said he has no intention to order direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to tackle the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent rebound, in a rare move for a Japanese official to publicly rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a sharp appreciation.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's GDP Grows 0.8%\par \par \uc2 The South Korean economy improved in the first quarter from the prior three months, but at a slightly slower pace than previously forecast.\par \par \uc2 North Korea Will Resume Hotline With South\par \par \uc2 North Korea has suggested it is prepared to reinstate communication channels, Korean Central News Agency said. They were largely cut off by the North earlier this year following the imposition of sanctions on the North for its Feb. 12 nuclear test.\par \par \uc2 ECB Rules Out Stimulus, Despite Poorer Outlook\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took no new steps to boost the euro zone's flagging economic prospects despite forecasting an even-deeper recession this year and low inflation in 2014, putting its stimulus tools "on the shelf."\par \par \uc2 Soros Fund Back in Japan Market\par \par \uc2 Investors of all types are selling Japanese stocks, worried a recovery might not be easy for the government to engineer. But \uc2 George Soros\uc2 's firm, \uc2 Soros Fund Management\uc2 , is buying once again [ 07-06-13 1008GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020130607e96700007\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
