\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Philippine peso up despite c.bank move; baht at 16-year high\b0\par\par\uc2 1,389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2013\par 03:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * BSP eases \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules to spur dlr buying, contain peso upside\par \par \uc2 * Short-covering, stock inflows, BOP support Philippine peso\par \par \uc2 * Won gains on exporters' demand; \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  eyed\par \par \uc2 * Baht at another fresh high, but profit-taking limits\par \par \uc2 (Adds text, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, April 19 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso rose on Friday as investors covered short positions even as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced steps to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's upside, while continuing inflows lifted the Thai baht to a fresh 16-year high although some traders booked profits.\par \par \uc2 The peso rose 0.4 percent to 41.07 per dollar as it received more support from an improving balance of payments and from demand linked to Thursday's stock inflows, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The country had a $452 million balance of payments surplus in March, compared with a $960 million deficit in February, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the \uc2 Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  liberalised rules on foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions, allowing residents to invest in property abroad and offshore funds.\par \par \uc2 But the measures are unlikely to have an immediate impact on the peso and they have been priced in because of previous and repeated comments by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, traders and analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts said the Philippines will see more inflows, given its strong economic growth and stable inflation.\par \par \uc2 "We think these measures will take time before they start having visible impact on the peso," \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "To the extent that Philippines remain attractive to overseas investors, and the economy continues to outperform, we think that these measures will not be enough to induce significant outflows in the near term," it added.\par \par \uc2 The Philippine economy is expected to expand 6.0 percent this year, the second fastest pace after 6.4 percent for Indonesia, the \uc2 Asian Development Bank\uc2  said this month.\par \par \uc2 But Philippine annual inflation is forecast at 3.6 percent, much lower than 5.2 percent seen for Southeast Asia's largest economy, according to the ADB.\par \par \uc2 The peso has eased 0.1 percent against the dollar this year, according to Thomson Reuters data, as investors took profit from the second best performer among emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2012, with a 6.8 percent gain.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem the peso's appreciation, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors also reduced bullish bets on the peso and bonds to book profits after a long-awaited ratings upgrade. In late March, \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  raised the Philippines' credit rating to an investment grade.\par \par \uc2 Even though the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures may not drag the peso lower for now, it is not free from fragile global risk sentiment, traders said.\par \par \uc2 "We should see the 41.00 level trying to hold for now, especially with global economic data waning," said a foreign bank trader in Manila.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The South Korean won ended local trade up 0.7 percent against the dollar, outperforming regional peers, as exporters' demand caused some investors to cover short positions, traders said.\par \par \uc2 But its upside was limited as the yen slipped after Japanese Finance Minister Taro Aso said the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  has accepted the country's explanation that its aggressive monetary easing is aimed at beating deflation and not at competitively weakening the yen.\par \par \uc2 The two countries compete in key overseas markets and a softer yen is seen hurting South Korea's exporters.\par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the won gained 1.3 percent to 11.2512, its strongest since October 2008.\par \par \uc2 That increased caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities, although the won may extend gains with the coming month-end likely to boost exporters' demand, traders said.\par \par \uc2 "The authorities will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the yen/won. But the won is expected to rise further from next week as everybody is tired of trying to weaken it now," said a senior foreign bank trader in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The baht rose as much as 0.3 percent to 28.63 per dollar, its strongest since 1997 on sustained inflows.\par \par \uc2 But some of the gains were erased as investors took profits, seeing the best performing Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year as excessively bought.\par \par \uc2 The 14-day dollar/baht's relative strength index stood at 25.1, still lower than the 30-threshold. An index reading below 30 indicates a pair is technically oversold.\par \par \uc2 The baht has gained 1.2 percent against the dollar this week, extending its 2013 appreciation to 6.8 percent, according to Thomson Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  Governor Prasarn Trairatvorakul has until recently been fairly relaxed about the baht's rise, saying it was catching up with the appreciation of other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But on April 9, he said it was rising too rapidly and on Friday he told reporters: "I feel that (the baht at this level) is a bit beyond fundamentals."\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Kittirat Na Ranong has put pressure on the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  to cut interest rates in an attempt to make the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  less attractive. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in part because of concern about an increase in household debt, has left the policy rate at 2.75 percent since October.\par \par \uc2 Kittirat was asked at a debate on Thursday evening if he had thought about sacking the governor. He replied: "I have had such a thought. In fact, it's just a thought."\par \par \uc2 The government nominates the governor but he is formally appointed by the king and according to the \uc2 Bank of Thailand Act\uc2  can only be removed for misconduct, the "dishonest performance of duties", gross incompetence or incapacity.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Kittirat reiterated that he wanted to see lower interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "Don't think that I want a lower rate in order to boost domestic investment. But it's because the higher spread on Thai interest rates has led to inflows to seek returns," he told reporters.\par \par \uc2 TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar advanced up to 0.4 percent to 29.788 against the greenback, its strongest since March 25, as local shares outperformed most Asian bourses with a 1.8 percent gain.\par \par \uc2 The island's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also found support on inflows from foreign financial institutions, although the volume was smaller than on Thursday, traders in Taipei said.\par \par \uc2 But the trading was not so active, with exporters inclined to wait for better levels to buy the Taiwan dollar for settlements.\par \par \uc2 Taiwan's export orders for March, due on Monday, will be in focus.\par \par \uc2 The exports orders probably grew again in March after a contraction the previous month, a Reuters poll showed, which would indicate that recovery of the export-driven economy and the health of Asia tech products demand remain on track.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0730 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        99.10          98.14       -0.97\par  Sing dlr        1.2352         1.2359       +0.06\par  Taiwan dlr      29.792         29.910       +0.40\par  Korean won     1115.78        1124.00       +0.74\par  Baht             28.67          28.72       +0.17\par  Peso             41.07          41.22       +0.37\par  Rupiah         9710.00        9712.00       +0.02\par  Rupee            53.96          53.96       +0.00\par  Ringgit         3.0345         3.0340       -0.02\par  Yuan            6.1789         6.1813       +0.04\par  Change so far in 2013\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        99.10          86.79      -12.42\par  Sing dlr        1.2352         1.2219       -1.08\par  Taiwan dlr      29.792         29.136       -2.20\par  Korean won [20130419 014123 GMT]   \par    1115.78        1070.60       -4.05\par  Baht             28.67          30.61       +6.77\par  Peso             41.07          41.05       -0.05\par  Rupiah         9710.00        9630.00       -0.82\par  Rupee            53.96          54.99       +1.91\par  Ringgit         3.0345         3.0580       +0.77\par  Yuan            6.1789         6.2303       +0.83\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Emily Chan in TAIPEI, Kitiphong Thaichare