\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won slides on weaker yen, Sing dlr dips on tame inflation\b0\par\par\uc2 1,103 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2013\par 02:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Singapore Jan CPI +3.6 pct y/y; below expectations\par \par \uc2  * Won dips on offshore funds selling; exporters cap downside\par \par \uc2  * Rupiah edges down on local corp dlr demand \par \par \uc2 (Adds text, updates prices)\par \par \uc2  By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Feb 25 (Reuters) - The won slid on Monday as investors worried about the impact of a fresh fall in the yen on South Korea's export competitiveness while other emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under pressure on weaker Chinese data.\par \par \uc2  The yen hit a 33-month low against the dollar as speculation increased that the Japanese government was very likely to name two strong supporters of aggressive monetary easing to top posts at the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Investors were also keeping an eye on Federal Reserve Chairman \uc2 Ben Bernanke\uc2 's comments later this week for clues on whether and when the Fed may scale back its asset-buying programme.\par \par \uc2  If the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps back from its easing policy, it will prompt investors to unwind long positions in emerging Asian assets, traders said.\par \par \uc2  "The Fed and BOJ dynamics are important constraints to Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Sacha Tihanyi, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for Scotiabank in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2  Weaker Chinese purchasing managers data that showed the country's vast manufacturing sector pulled back from two-year highs also weighed on sentiment.\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar fell after the city-state reported a slower-than-expected inflation rate in January, but later recovered some losses. \par \par \uc2  Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have eased so far this year as the yen dropped and on concern that the Fed may wind down monetary easing sooner than expected.\par \par \uc2  But one analyst said the regional units are unlikely to weaken much further if the BOJ carries out actual easing.\par \par \uc2  "As we have gone through quite some sessions of correction already, further reaction may be muted unless BOJ indeed embarks on a new round of easing," said Frances Cheung, senior strategist at \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  CIB in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2  WON\par \par \uc2  The won eased as some offshore funds sold it on a weaker yen and a retreat in China's \uc2 HSBC\uc2  flash purchasing managers' index (PMI), traders said. Importers also bought dollars for payments.\par \par \uc2  The South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, recovered some of earlier losses on exporters' demand for month-end settlements.\par \par \uc2  Domestic exporters are likely to snap up the won around 1,090 per dollar, traders said.\par \par \uc2  "Exporter deals are likely to support the won this week. But the authorities may step in the market if the yen tumbles further," said a senior foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2  Seoul \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities have been expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the competitiveness of its export-oriented firms. \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japan compete in key export markets. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  Besides the inflation data, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also fell on profit taking.\par \par \uc2  "The Singapore dollar may weaken more if the yen falls further and the euro drops," said a senior Asian bank trader.\par \par \uc2  "It is possible to see 1.2410. But no more than that," said the trader, noting that other emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  haven't fallen much on the day.\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar has a 200-day moving average at 1.2408. Once that level is broken again, it may weaken to 1.2465, the 38.2 percent Fibonacci retracement of its appreciation between June and October, according to analysts. On Feb 21, it closed weaker than the average for the first time since June.\par \par \uc2  Earlier on Monday, it hit 1.2407 to the U.S. dollar and threatened to go past the average.\par \par \uc2  On Friday, stronger-than-expected growth data helped the city-state's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  enjoy a 0.4 percent gain against the greenback, its largest daily percentage appreciation since Jan. 10, according to Thomson Reuters data.\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar depreciated as investors covered short-positions in the U.S. dollar before Singapore announced its budget later in the day.\par \par \uc2  RUPIAH\par \par \uc2  The rupiah edged lower on month-end dollar demand from local companies, while state-run lenders and foreign banks bought the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , limiting its downside.\par \par \uc2  Investors have not responded yet to the government's surprising nomination of the finance minister as the next \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor.\par \par \uc2  Indonesia's president has unexpectedly nominated Finance Minister Agus Martowardojo as the sole candidate to be the next \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor of Southeast Asia's largest economy, a parliament official told Reuters on Friday. \par \par \uc2  But Martowardojo ran into opposition on Monday, as one member of a parliamentary commission that has the final word on selection questioned his integrity and another doubted his grasp of macroeconomics. \par \par \uc2  Some expected the appointment to support sentiment on Indonesia, saying a change may well be order given the current account deficit and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reluctance to raise rates.\par \par \uc2  But traders doubt how much support the rupiah would receive from the move.\par \par \uc2  "His background as a banker definitely made him more familiar with handling inflation through rate policies," said a Jakarta-based trader.\par \par \uc2  "But it is very complicated to gauge what is happening to the rupiah. Now we are feeling the effect of the global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war. Imports increased in multitude due to cheap goods," said the trader.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  Change on the day at 0710 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        94.25          93.49       -0.81\par  Sing dlr        1.2383         1.2372       -0.09\par  Taiwan dlr      29.655         29.658       +0.01\par  Korean won     1086.00        1084.70       -0.12\par *Baht             29.84          29.86       +0.05\par  Peso             40.70          40.69       -0.01\par  Rupiah         9710.00        9708.00       -0.02\par  Rupee            54.05          54.18       +0.23\par  Ringgit         3.0990         3.1015       +0.08\par  Yuan            6.2338         6.2351       +0.02\par  Change so far in 2013\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        94.25          86.79       -7.92\par  Sing dlr        1.2383         1.2219       -1.32\par  Taiwan dlr      29.655         29.136       -1.75\par  Korean won     1086.00        1070.60       -1.42\par  Baht             29.84          30.61       +2.58\par  Peso             40.70          41.05       +0.87\par  Rupiah         9710.00        9630.00       -0.82\par  Rupee     