\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won up despite tighter  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  rules; Philippine peso at 4-1/2-yr high\b0\par\par\uc2 1,104 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2012\par 02:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * S.Korea to reduce limits on banks' \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives holdings\par \par \uc2  * Exporters, offshore funds support won\par \par \uc2  * Philippine peso up on remittances, stop-loss dlr selling\par \par \uc2  * Taiwan dlr higher on exporters, inflows\par \par \uc2  * Philippine, Singapore, Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  spotted-dealers \par \par \uc2 (Adds text, updates prices)\par \par \uc2  By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 27 (Reuters) - The South Korean won rose despite tougher rules and the Philippine peso hit its strongest level in more than four-and-a-half years on Tuesday with a Greek deal supporting emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted capping the upside.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided to cut ceilings on foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives positions of banks and warned it could take additional steps to stem hot money inflows that have pushed up the value of the won. \par \par \uc2  Despite the move, the won crawled higher on demand from offshore funds and exporters.\par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso gained on remittance inflows and stop-loss dollar selling. The Taiwan dollar  advanced thanks to exporters and inflows from foreign financial institutions. Dealers said they spotted the central banks of Philippines and Taiwan were spotted buying U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  Regional stocks and the euro also rose after a deal on new debt targets for Greece and a political agreement on disbursing the next installment of aid was announced.\par \par \uc2  "I will keep long positions in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as long as the euro stays above 1.2950," said a senior Malaysian bank dealer in Kuala Lumpur. The euro hovered around 1.2990 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2  Still, emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are seen vulnerable to possible corrections as the agreement has been priced in regional units, some dealers and analysts said.\par \par \uc2  In addition to regional authorities' steps to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation, investors are wary of the U.S. "fiscal cliff" of steep tax increases and spending cuts which could push Asia's major export market into recession.    \par \par \uc2  Republicans and Democrats were still at odds as Congress returned from its Thanksgiving holiday break. \par \par \uc2  "There is little momentum to push up Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  more from here, although it is hard to doubt that there is a long-term bullish trend in the improving U.S. and Chinese economies," said Yuna Park, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond analyst at \uc2 Dongbu Securities\uc2  in Seoul.\par \par \uc2  "Some of them are likely to suffer from short-term corrections on potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fiscal cliff worries," said Park, adding that recent outperformers such as the Philippine peso were likely to fall more.\par \par \uc2  The peso was the best-performing emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year with a 7.2 percent gain against the dollar so far.\par \par \uc2  WON\par \par \uc2  The won gained as offshore funds took the announcement of the tighter regulations as chances to buy it on dips. Exporters joined the bids.\par \par \uc2  Investors have prepared for the measures and the announcement cleared uncertainty over the rules, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  Still, investors stayed cautious over possible dollar-purchases by the authorities for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That caused domestic importers to buy dollars for payments.\par \par \uc2  "Actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  became more important. But they will defend the 1,080 no matter what happens," said a senior foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2  "They need to do something on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the economy as other countries are easing policies," he added.\par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO\par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso hit 40.870 per dollar, its strongest since March 2008, as investors dumped greenbacks to stop losses after the 41.000 was broken.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted buying dollars to slow down the peso's strength, repeating its recent warnings, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  "Peso appreciation is driven more by fundamental flows like exports, tourist receipts, remittances and BPO (business process outsourcing) revenues," Deputy Governor Diwa Guinigundo said in a text message. \par \par \uc2  "BSP is of course conscious of the possible fallout in terms of lower external competitiveness... will continue to check the remaining space for \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulatory liberalization," he added, referring to \uc2 Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Some investors took profits with some short-term peso forwards quoted at a discount.\par \par \uc2  "The market seems to be a bit cautious in selling spot dollar lower as onshore points are softer and the euro's upward momentum may have slowed," said a foreign bank dealer in Manila.\par \par \uc2  Investors are keeping an eye on the country's third quarter growth data due on Wednesday for clues on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy meeting in December.\par \par \uc2  Philippine economic growth likely defied the global downdraft and picked up modestly in the third quarter thanks to strong domestic demand and a late spurt in exports, a Reuters poll showed. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar rose on exporters' demand for settlements and as foreign financial institutions bought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Greece deal.\par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted buying U.S. dollars to stem the island's unit around 29.050-29.070 to the greenback, limiting the Taiwan dollar's upside, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar barely changed as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  The city-state's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  initially strengthened to 1.2207 to the U.S. dollar, but agent banks of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore were spotted buying U.S. dollars at around that level,\par \par \uc2 the dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \par \par \uc2  Change on the day at 0645 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        82.26          82.07       -0.24\par  Sing dlr        1.2213         1.2213       +0.00\par  Taiwan dlr      29.083         29.143       +0.21\par  Korean won     1084.00        1085.50       +0.14\par  Baht             30.67          30.69       +0.07\par  Peso             40.90          41.00       +0.24\par  Rupiah         9600.00        9595.00       -0.05\par  Rupee            55.70          55.73       +0.05\par  Ringgit         3.0500         3.0545       +0.15\par  Yuan            6.2223         6.2255       +0.05\par  Change so far in 2012\par  \f28 \b \h