\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/KRW Remains Lower; 1,100-1,103 Band Eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 165 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2012\par 04:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0241 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/KRW remains slightly lower at 1,101.80 vs 1,103.60 late Wednesday in Seoul, with exporters and offshore players looking to sell into any rebound, traders say. The pair, however, continues to hover around 1,101, unable to break lower levels as players remain remain wary of a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 /government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister Bahk Jae-wan says the government is closely monitoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The pair is heavily biased to the downside and the chance of USD-buying BOK \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be the only reason keeping the pair from falling further, says a foreign bank trader. He tips the pair to stay in a tight 1,100-1,103 range. (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 [ 25-10-12 0241GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1012 1063 1085 1858 5029 55112 75112   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121025e8ap00049\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
