\par\par \b \uc2 South Korea Won Rises to 6-Month High; Bonds Down\b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2012\par 10:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                     Close    Change \par  USD/KRW            1,116.00 -1.20 \par  JPY/KRW            14.2529  -0.1496 \par  3-Year Treasurys   2.90%    +4 bps \par  5-Year Treasurys   2.97%    +4 bps \par  10-Year Treasurys  3.13%    +5 bps \par  20-Year Treasurys  3.14%    +5 bps \par  \par    By Kwanwoo Jun \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SEOUL--The South Korean won rose to a six-month high against the U.S. dollar late Monday, extending gains after the U.S Federal Reserve unveiled new stimulus last week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at KRW1,116.00--its lowest since KRW1,115.50 on March 2--compared with KRW1,117.20 late Friday in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 The U.S dollar fell as low as KRW1,113.00 before bouncing back, as players were testing whether \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the event of sharp gains in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar, said traders and market watchers.\par \par \uc2 "The tremor of the U.S. Federal Reserve's (third round of quantitative easing, or QE3,) continues to run today, with the dollar still in the process of falling," said Woori Futures \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst Byeon Ji-young.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Byeon said the dollar, however, would find strong support at KRW1,100, a crucial level that local authorities don't want the pair to breach.\par \par \uc2 She said she expects the dollar to trade in a range of KRW1,110-KRW1,118 this week.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said dollar selling related to foreigners' local-stock purchases added to the greenback's losses earlier in the session, as there were no signs of South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money markets.\par \par \uc2 Given possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market participants are likely to retreat to the sidelines, they said.\par \par \uc2 Government bonds and bond futures were lower, following the U.S. Federal Reserve's move to buy more mortgage-backed bonds.\par \par \uc2 Investors were wary of bonds after recent sharp losses, and have turned to riskier assets following the Fed's stimulus, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 September bond futures ended 10 ticks lower at 105.87.\par \par \uc2 Write to Kwanwoo Jun at kwanwoo.jun@dowjones.com [ 17-09-12 0810GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1063 1858   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120917e89h000en\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
