\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Ringgit, won lead Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  gains; wary of  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,145 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 2012\par 03:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Ringgit up on unwinding bearish bets vs Sing dlr\par \par \uc2 * Won hits 4-mth high on stock inflows\par \par \uc2 * Sing dlr stable amid \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk\par \par \uc2 (Adds text, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 1 (Reuters) - The Malaysian ringgit and the South Korean won led gains among emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, but the upside was limited by qualms that authorities in the region would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervence\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains amid a slowing global economy.\par \par \uc2 The ringgit enjoyed demand against the Singapore dollar , while the won hit a near four-month high against the dollar on continuous stock inflows and exporters' bids for settlements.\par \par \uc2 Still, investors were reluctant to raise their bets in emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as data across the region, including a weak Chinese manufacturing indicator, suggested a synchronised slowdown.\par \par \uc2 Investors kept an eye on the likely outcome of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's policy meeting later in the day, remaining wary of the\par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gathering on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Hopes faded for bold stimulus action by the major central banks appear to have faded. The Fed is widely expected to refrain from a third round of quantitative easing this time, although it will emphasize its commitment to maintaining easy policy and could signal that further stimulus steps are coming.\par \par \uc2 "With the market well biased to expect something out of the Fed over the next 24 hours, a decision to not undertake any additional easing measures like an extension of verbal rate guidance will provide a broad boost for the greenback and take a good deal of steam out of the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  space," said Sacha Tihanyi, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for Scotiabank in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 After the Fed, the ECB will be in the spotlight, especially after ECB President \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  said last week that he would do whatever it takes to save the euro.\par \par \uc2 Market anticipation of further action from Europe, such as bond buying by the euro zone's rescue funds, has already waned somewhat amid continued objections from Germany.\par \par \uc2 Germany's finance ministry\uc2  on Tuesday reiterated its view that there was no need to grant a banking license to the euro zone's new bailout fund. Such a license could enable the fund to buy virtually unlimited amounts of debt issued by troubled euro zone states.\par \par \uc2 Growing evidence of slowing Asian economies were another curb on investor appetite for regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 China's official factory purchasing managers' index fell to an eight-month low of 50.1 in July, while manufacturing activity in South Korea and Taiwan deteriorated.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won rose as much as 0.5 percent to 1,125.1 per dollar, its strongest since April 3 on sustained demand from custodian banks after foreign investors' massive purchases of Seoul shares .\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have bought a combined net 1.6 trillion Korean won ($1.4 billion) in local stocks since Friday, according to Korea Exchange data.\par \par \uc2 Domestic exporters and offshore funds joined bids for the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.\par \par \uc2 But interbank speculators were cautious over possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities to slow down the local unit's strength.\par \par \uc2 "The authorities may be inclined to defend the exchange rates as exports were in such bad shape and there is no inflationary pressure," said a senior foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 South Korean exports in July suffered the worst showing in nearly three years, while inflation last month slid to a 12-year plus low, the government data showed earlier.\par \par \uc2 RINGGIT\par \par \uc2 The ringgit gained 0.2 percent to 2.5024 against the Singapore dollar as investors continued to unwind bearish positions in the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus its neighbor's unit.\par \par \uc2 The ringgit is seen having resistance around 2.5000 versus the Singapore dollar. The gain against the Singapore dollar helped the ringgit hit 3.1110 versus the U.S. dollar, its strongest since May 22.\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar was barely changed against the U.S. dollar on caution over potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There was a market talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore was spotted at 1.2431 versus the greenback, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah slid on dollar demand from oil companies and local banks, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered some of initial slide as real foreign banks bought it with some demand from real money funds, they added.\par \par \uc2 Investors were awaiting announcements from major central banks -- the Fed and the ECB -- but the rupiah has priced hopes of their stimulus much in, dealers said, citing continuous bids for the Indonesian unit from foreign banks.\par \par \uc2 PHILIPPINE PESO\par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso eased as interbank speculators took profits. Short-term traders stayed on the sidelines, keeping an eye on outcomes results from the Fed and ECB meetings.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Philippines \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the peso could strengthen further on strong dollar inflows as investors take advantage of a favorable economic outlook.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0710 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        78.11          78.12       +0.01\par  Sing dlr        1.2445         1.2450       +0.04\par  Taiwan dlr      29.968         30.010       +0.14\par  Korean won     1126.04        1130.60       +0.40\par  Baht             31.45          31.53       +0.25\par  Peso             41.77          41.72       -0.11\par  Rupiah         9460.00        9440.00       -0.21\par  Rupee            55.48          55.65       +0.31\par  Ringgit         3.1150         3.1305       +0.50\par  Yuan            6.3704         6.3627       -0.12\par  Change so far in 2012\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        78.11          76.92       -1.53\par  Sing dlr        1.2445         1.2969       +4.21\par  Taiwan dlr      29.968         30.290       +1.07\par  Korean won     1126.04        1151.80       +2.29\par  Baht             31.45          31.55       +0.32\par  Peso             41.77          43.84       +4.97\par  Rupiah         9460.00        9060.00       -4.23\par  Rupee            55.48          53.08       -4.32\par  Ringgit         3.1150         3.1685       +1.7