\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Short-covering lifts Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , RBI boosts rupee\b0\par\par\uc2 1,031 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2012\par 07:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * RBI estimated to have sold up to $500 mln -dealers\par \par \uc2 * S.Korea fin min says won's recent move excessive\par \par \uc2 * Sing dlr up on real money interest, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  caution\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, May 15 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee rose on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying, leading a rebound among emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday as investors covered short positions on strong German growth data and expectations regional authorities could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support their units.\par \par \uc2 The German economy grew 0.5 percent in the first quarter on strong exports, well above market forecasts, helping the euro and other risky assets rebound.\par \par \uc2 Still, investors hesitated to add bets on emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on growing fears that Greece may exit the euro zone amid political uncertainty.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell with the Indian rupee sliding to near a record low prior to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying, and the South Korean won was at its weakest in about four months.\par \par \uc2 Regional units are expected to stay weak as investors are likely to shun risk positions on intensifying fears over Greece, analysts and dealers said.\par \par \uc2 "Nothing has been changed. The rebound is a just shallow one, although we may see bigger short-covering," said a senior Malaysian bank dealer in Kuala Lumpur. "All the problems remain unsolved unless we get an announcement from Greece."\par \par \uc2 Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been under pressure as investors feared that political uncertainty in the euro zone may derail austerity measures and devastate the continent's effort to tackle its debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 Greek party leaders are expected to convene later on Tuesday but there is little hope that President Karolos Papoulias's proposal to form a technocrat government will end a political the stalemate, and the most likely outcome would be a new election.\par \par \uc2 Suresh Kumar Ramanathan, regional rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at CIMB Investment Bank in Kuala Lumpur, said emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have so far priced in only a "very minimal" amount of risk relating to Greece.\par \par \uc2 "The directional trade is short EUR/USD, long USD/AXJ and rather mixed in EUR/AXJ," Ramanathan said.\par \par \uc2 The global economic outlook also stayed dim.\par \par \uc2 China's foreign direct investment inflows fell in the first four months of the year, data showed, another signs showing that the world's second-largest economy is slowing.\par \par \uc2 RUPEE\par \par \uc2 Dollar/rupee slid as the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India (RBI) \uc2 was estimated to have sold up to $500 million in spot for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although some of that was possibly also in forward markets, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could step into the market again as it looks to defend the pair at 54.00, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 Dollar/won rose to as high as 1,156.8, the highest since Jan. 12 on stock outflows and bids from offshore funds.\par \par \uc2 But the pair could not rise further, with resistance at 1,157.0, the 61.8 percent Fibonacci retracement of its December-March slide, and on caution over dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan said the won's recent movements were excessive relative to the country's fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors were net sellers in Seoul's main exchange\par \par \uc2 for a 10th consecutive session, and have shed a net 2.2 trillion won ($1.91 billion) during that period.\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 U.S. dollar/Singapore dollar turned lower as real money investors and European investors sold it as the pair failed to stay above a technical resistance at 1.2587, the top of an Ichimoku cloud. The pair had been below the top since mid-January.\par \par \uc2 Investors stayed cautious over possible U.S. dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks to check inflationary pressure.\par \par \uc2 PHILIPPINE PESO\par \par \uc2 Dollar/peso hit a near five-week high of 42.83, but the pair turned lower on remittance inflows, while local banks took profits around a Fibonacci resistance, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Some local names sold the pair above 42.800, near the 61.8 percent retracement at 42.803 of its March-April slide, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 Foreign banks continued to buy dollar/rupiah, while the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted limiting its gains, dealers said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0800 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        79.92          79.85       -0.09\par  Sing dlr        1.2549         1.2575       +0.21\par  Taiwan dlr      29.458 