\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 877 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2012\par 05:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: AUSTRALIA'S GILLARD WINS PARTY CHALLENGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prime Minister Julia Gillard held off a leadership challenge from rival Kevin Rudd on Monday, setting the stage for a bid to reunite her divided party and win back disenchanted voters. (published 0054 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S PM GILLARD SAYS UNITED LABOR CAN WIN NEXT ELECTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prime Minister Julia Gillard said Monday that her minority Labor government will move forward as a united team and can win the next general election, after she defeated former leader Kevin Rudd's challenge for the party leadership. (published 0251 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: G-20: EU REHN: HOPE TO MAKE DECISION ON IMF RESOURCE INCREASE AT APRIL MEETING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European Union hopes to see non-euro-zone countries increase their contributions to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  to help it stem its debt crisis by the IMF meetings in April, the EU's economics chief said Sunday. (published 0024 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: IMF CHIEF: FUNDS COULD BE QUICKLY RAISED, FLEXIBLE ON AMOUNT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cash to boost \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  lending resources could be quickly raised once Europe boosts it emergency rescue facility, the head of the fund said Sunday. (published 0117 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN LIKELY TO LEAD THE WAY IN SUPPORT FOR IMF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan is showing willingness to be among the first countries to boost financial support for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  to help tackle the European debt crisis, as Tokyo seeks a quick end to global financial turmoil that has pushed the yen to record highs. (published 0149 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: G-20: DRAGHI SEES RETURN OF MARKET CONFIDENCE IN EURO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financial markets are regaining confidence in the euro following the bloc's "vast" reform effort, European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Mario Draghi said Sunday, although he warned that credit conditions are still tightening even after the ECB's first ever three-year loan. (published 0151 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: GERMAN INTERIOR MINISTER URGES GREEK EXIT FROM EURO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chancellor Angela Merkel's effort to rally the German people behind her strategy for saving Greece and the euro suffered a blow over the weekend after a senior member of her government said Athens should be encouraged to leave the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bloc. (published 2155 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INTERVIEW: BOK \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVE CHIEF: TO BEGIN CHINA BOND PURCHASES IN 1H \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plans to start buying Chinese securities in the first half of this year in a move to diversify its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves--the world's seventh largest--and benefit from the yuan's rise as a potential reserve \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a senior Bank of Korea official said. (published 0319 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ INTERVIEW: S KOREA OPPOSITION PARTY POLICYMAKER: GOVERNMENT SHOULDN'T \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's government shouldn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market unless it is "seriously compromised by speculative forces," the chief policymaker of the main opposition Democratic United Party said. (published 0404 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: PBOC GAUGES DEMAND FOR 3-MONTH BILL SALES THIS WEEK - TRADERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday gauged demand from banks for a routine three-month bill offering this week, indicating it may resume the sale of such bills after a two-month suspension, traders participating in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said. (published 0315 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: NEW ZEALAND POSTS TRADE DEFICIT, DAIRY EXPORTS REMAIN STRONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's January monthly trade balance swung into a deficit even as agricultural exports held up, and economists continue to expect moderation in the annual surplus going forward. (published 0229 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA MANUFACTURERS' OUTLOOK INDEX FOR MARCH RISES TO 5-MONTH HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An index measuring South Korean manufacturers' outlook on business conditions in the coming month rose to its highest in five months, boosted by signs of improvement in Europe's sovereign debt crisis, a survey by the Bank of Korea showed Sunday. (published 2100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA BANK RATINGS AT RISK FROM ANY CHINA SLOWDOWN -S&P \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian bank ratings are at risk from any downturn in the nation's economy triggered by a "hard landing" in China, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ratings Services said Monday. (published 0211 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT BERAU COAL ENERGY\f28 \uc2 \f2  PLANS DOLLAR BOND AFTER ROADSHOW STARTING FEB 29 - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Berau Coal Energy\f28 \uc2 \f2  is planning to sell a benchmark dollar bond following a global roadshow starting Wednesday, a person familiar with the matter told Dow Jones Newswires Monday. (published 0257 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par HEARD ON THE STREET: DON'T DISMISS DEFAULT POSITION ON GREECE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For months, European policy makers railed against triggering credit-default swaps, or CDS, on Greek debt. Politicians have denounced the CDS market as a speculative vehicle exacerbating the crisis, although regulators have found no evidence of that being the case. But the voluntary Greek bond swap may yet end up triggering CDS--and that may be no bad thing. (published 1943 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: BIG BOND FUNDS DIVERGE ON EMERGING MARKETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some of the world's biggest bond-fund managers disagree on the future of the $2.3 trillion market for emerging-market debt, continuing the debate about the impact of the European crisis on global growth. (published 2137 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: INVESTORS TAKE A SHINE TO 'JUNK' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors of all stripes are once again piling into "junk" bonds. (published 2104 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 27-02-12 0407GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120227e82r0005y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
