\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Taiwan dlr leads Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  gains, rupiah down on rate cut\b0\par\par\uc2 1,130 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2012\par 06:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Taiwan dlr up as foreigners keep buying stocks\par \par \uc2 * Taiwan c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  spotted, but size smaller -traders\par \par \uc2 * Won turns slightly higher, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  caution cap\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Feb 9 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar hit a five-month high on Thursday, leading gains in many of its Asian peers, on hopes that Greece was nearing a deal that could pave the way for fresh international aid, but the rupiah extended losses after a surprise interest rate cut by Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Greek political leaders have agreed on all points demanded by its international lenders except one -- pension cuts -- and officials said discussions would continue so a deal could be concluded before a meeting of euro zone finance ministers on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Hopes that a deal would be reached, allowing Athens to avoid a potentially chaotic debt default, also powered the euro to a two-month highs on the dollar and the yen.\par \par \uc2 Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely to remain firm as investors bring more money to Asia, analysts and dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Underlining this view, pressure on emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from a pick-up in China's inflation did not last long.\par \par \uc2 "The data did not indicate a policy shift to tightening and other recent data from Asia was not that bad," said Jeong My-young, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Samsung Futures in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 "Upcoming economic data holds a key, but as long as the data does not point to a sharp slowdown, we will see sustained inflows," Jeong added, noting global markets remain flush with liquidity.\par \par \uc2 Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have appreciated this year, fuelled by high liquidity, signs that the euro zone's debt crisis is easing and a spate of data showing the U.S. economy is gathering momentum.\par \par \uc2 But their gains have been checked by frequent setbacks in Greek aid and debt restructuring talks, and by caution that regional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising too fast.\par \par \uc2 Many of them are also around technical resistance lines, with the South Korean won facing a 200-day moving average at 1,110 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Euro/dollar has overpriced the conclusion of the Greek debt discussion, which has yet to reach a consensus, thus the unwinding of long euro positions has a knock-on effect on Asia-ex Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Suresh Kumar Ramanathan, regional rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for CIMB Investment Bank in Kuala Lumpur.\par \par \uc2 TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 U.S. dollar/Taiwan dollar slid to as low as 29.410, the weakest since Sept 13, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted buying only small amount of the pair and foreign banks sold it, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors were net buyers of the island's stocks for a fourth consecutive session, bringing their total net purchases so far this month to T$31.6 billion Taiwan dollar ($1.07 billion).\par \par \uc2 Traders estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have purchased about $100 million-$200 million during the day, which they said was smaller than the "usual" daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  size.\par \par \uc2 Taiwanese oil importers bought the pair below 29.45 where they had bought it in the last two weeks, dealers said. Their bids caused short-covering.\par \par \uc2 Investors stayed wary of possible steps by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit its slide.\par \par \uc2 On late Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor fired a warning over hot money, reminding foreign investors of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rule that money they bring into Taiwan must be used to buy stocks.\par \par \uc2 In remarks to local reporters, Perng Fai-nan said that although the fundamentals across Asian countries were different, exchange rates and stock markets were moving in the same direction, indicating the arrival of "hot money".\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 Dollar/won turned lower on exporters supplies and as a firm euro spurred stop-loss sales.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, the pair rose on short-covering amid caution over possible dollar-demand linked to Lone Star's sale of a stake in \uc2 Korea Exchange Bank\uc2  to \uc2 Hana Financial Group\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Investors see further slides in dollar/won, but more players are wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities.\par \par \uc2 Some dealers suspected of their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 1,115.\par \par \uc2 "There were strong bids around 1,115 and few players would attack the level. It is hard to build up aggressive short positions here as the authorities put lower fluctuation as a top priority," said a local bank dealer.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players ignored the Bank of Korea's decision to leave interest rates unchanged as it has been widely expected.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 Dollar/rupiah extended gains after Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unexpectedly cut its policy rate by 25 bps.\par \par \uc2 The pair rose as much as 1.3 percent to 8,982 from 8,920 before the surprising decision.\par \par \uc2 One-month dollar/rupiah non-deliverable forward (NDF) edged down for the day, but the NDF briefly rose after the rate cut.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0740 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        77.18          77.05       -0.17\par  Sing dlr        1.2441         1.2467       +0.21\par  Taiwan dlr      29.438         29.530       +0.31\par  Korean won     1115.20        1115.80       +0.05\par  Baht             30.74          30.73       -0.03\par  Peso             42.16          42.22       +0.13\par  Rupiah         8980.00        8870.00       -1.22\par  Rupee            49.33          49.15       -0.36\par  Ringgit         3.0075         3.0033       -0.14\par  Yuan            6.2945         6.2945       +0.00\par  Change so far in 2012\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        77.18          76.92       -0.34\par  Sing dlr        1.2441         1.2969       +4.24\par  Taiwan dlr      29.438         30.290       +2.89\par  Korean won     1115.20        1151.80       +3.28\par  Baht             30.74          31.55       +2.64\par  Peso             42.16          43.84       +3.98\par  Rupiah         8980.00        9060.00       +0.89\par  Rupee            49.33          53.08       +7.60\par  Ringgit         3.0075         3.1685       +5.3