\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -C.banks' liquidity move lifts Asian  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; importers cap\b0\par\par\uc2 1,002 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 2011\par 05:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Won up 1.5 pct as foreigners keep buying stocks\par \par \uc2 * Talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Singapore, S.Korea\par \par \uc2 * Baht off high on Thai importers\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Dec 1 (Reuters) - The joint move by six top central banks to ease a liquidity crunch spurred rises for most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, but offers by offshore funds and Asian importers limited the gains.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the U.S. Federal Reserve, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the central banks of Canada, Britain, Japan and Switzerland said they would lower the cost of existing dollar swap lines by 50 basis points from Dec. 5, and arrange bilateral swaps to provide liquidity for other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The steps boosted riskier assets including stocks and the euro, prompting some hopes of new liquidity eventually coming to Asia.\par \par \uc2 "With the measures, we will see inflows to both stocks and bonds in Asia again, especially from long-term investors," said a senior Singaporean bank dealer.\par \par \uc2 Late last year and early this year, emerging Asian assets including \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  benefited from increased liquidity provided by central banks in developed countries.\par \par \uc2 Still, many investors doubted if liquidity newly provided by the major six central banks would come to Asia soon, given persistent doubt over effectiveness of efforts to cope with the European debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 The sovereign problems' impact on Asian economy is also getting more serious, keeping investors away from emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On Thursday, data showed that China's factory sector shrank in November, its first fall in nearly three years.\par \par \uc2 Investors are wary of possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by regional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities to maintain their countries' export competitiveness at a time economies are slowing.\par \par \uc2 There was market talk of such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Singapore and \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Agent banks of Singapore were seen at 1.2800 per dollar, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Frances Cheung, senior strategist for \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  CIB in Hong Kong, said she was looking to sell emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on rallies.\par \par \uc2 "The swap arrangement is among major central banks only. So there will not be liquidity directly flowing to Asia, although this action will surely boost sentiment, as this eases the liquidity pressure especially for European banks," she said.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, many investors took profits from early rises in the regional units rather than add to bets on them.\par \par \uc2 In November, emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell against the dollar on deepening worries about the euro zone's debt crisis, although they found relief from short covering this week.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 Dollar/won fell as foreign investors continued to scoop up Seoul shares, while South Korean importers and offshore funds bought the pair.\par \par \uc2 Some dealers said the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were spotted buying dollars almost all day long, while others doubted there was any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The pair opened at 1,123.0 and fell to as low as 1,122.0, a notch higher than the 61.8 percent Fibonacci retracement at 1,121.3 of its gains between late Oct and Nov.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think we will see massive inflows for now. We have few reasons to be too pessimistic, but it (the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move) does not mean that the world became beautiful again," said a foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 PHILIPPINE PESO\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Philippine peso slid with local banks selling, but some interbank speculators looked to buy the pair on possible USD-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The market is reacting to positive developments overnight, but there should be some support around 43.30," said a Manila-based European bank dealer, adding he'd like to buy the pair around that level.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 Dollar/baht fell, but its slide was limited as Thai importers bought the pair on dips, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Some interbank speculators looked to build up long dollar/baht positions, despite global major central banks' steps to ease the credit squeeze stemming from the euro zone's credit crisis.\par \par \uc2 "THB's rising momentum is fast, but I still love to add more USD/THB, since the latest move of the central banks is just temporary. The core problems are not yet solved," said a Bangkok-based dealer.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0745 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        77.62          77.63       +0.01\par  Sing dlr        1.2847         1.2813       -0.26\par  Taiwan dlr      30.110         30.345       +0.78\par  Korean won     1126.00        1143.00       +1.51\par  Baht             30.94          31.16       +0.71\par  Peso             43.29          43.64       +0.82\par  Rupiah         9090.00        9105.00       +0.17\par  Rupee            51.57          52.21       +1.24\par  Ringgit         3.1370         3.1795       +1.35\par  Yuan            6.3670         6.3789       +0.19\par  Change so far in 2011\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        77.62          81.15       +4.55\par  Sing dlr        1.2847         1.2820       -0.21\par  Taiwan dlr      30.110         30.368       +0.86\par  Korean won     1126.00        1134.80       +0.78\par  Baht             30.94          30.14       -2.59\par  Peso             43.29          43.84       +1.28\par  Rupiah         9090.00        9005.00       -0.94\par  Rupee            51.57          44.70      -13.31\par  Ringgit         3.1370         3.0820       -1.75\par  Yuan            6.3670         6.5897       +3.50\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Reuters \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Analyst Rick Lloyd and Catherine Tan of IFR Markets; Editing by Richard Borsuk)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the new Reuters scrolling global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  service please click\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Double click on brackets for following items: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2      Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Asia \tab \par Malaysian ringgit   Indonesian rupiah  \tab \par Singapore dollar    Thai baht          \tab \par Taiwan dollar       Hong Kong dollar   \tab \par Philippine peso      Korean won         \tab \par SPEED GUIDES  \tab \par Exotic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2      Non-G7 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 curr